  "BWA": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "UN reform",
        "text": "Supported UN80 but argued that efficiency savings should strengthen conflict prevention and delivery in program countries. Called for Security Council reform consistent with the common African position, including permanent representation for Africa and Latin America.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "President, Botswana supports reforms that strengthen the effectiveness, coherence, and responsiveness of the United Nations system."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "We also believe that efficiency gains should be redeployed to strengthen the capacity of the organization to prevent conflict, address emerging security threats, and deliver meaningful results in program countries in line with the UN80 vision."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "It is in this spirit that Botswana accords the highest priority to its partnerships with the United Nations Office of Counter-Terrorism, UN-Habitat, the International Trade Centre, the International Organization for Migration, among others."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "We particularly recognize UNOCT's leadership role in strengthening the United Nations' collective efforts to prevent and counter terrorism and violent extremism, and in translating international commitments into practical support for Member States."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "Botswana remains committed to further deepening its cooperation with UNOCT and the wider United Nations system through capacity-building, technical assistance, knowledge sharing, and the exchange of good practices."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "Such partnerships demonstrate that a responsive United Nations can build trust, strengthen national capacity, and foster peace and security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "President, no reform agenda, including UN80, is complete without addressing the longstanding inequities within the Security Council."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "In this regard, Botswana reaffirms its support for comprehensive Security Council reform and aligns itself with the common African position as articulated in the Ezulwini Consensus and the Sirte Declaration."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "We believe that a Security Council that continues to exclude Africa and Latin America from permanent membership cannot credibly claim to reflect contemporary geopolitical realities."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Health",
        "text": "Specifically called for preserving UNAIDS, citing its contribution to Botswana’s HIV response. Reported achievement of the 95-95-95 targets and offered to share lessons through South-South cooperation.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "President, health is where the promise of international solidarity is tested most directly, and Botswana speaks from hard-earned experience."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "Three decades ago, our country faced an HIV/AIDS pandemic of such severity that some questioned our long-term resilience."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "Through determined national leadership, bold public investment, and sustainable global partnership, Botswana built one of the world's most comprehensive HIV/AIDS treatment programs."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "We achieved the UNAIDS 95-95-95 targets ahead of schedule, and we became the first African country to achieve World Health Organization silver-tier status for the elimination of mother-to-child transmission of HIV."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "Our experience demonstrates that when national ownership and international solidarity converge, seemingly impossible challenges can be overcome."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "This kind of practical solidarity restores confidence in multilateralism."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "We stand ready to share the lessons of this experience through South-South and triangular cooperation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "Botswana attaches particular importance to preserving UNAIDS, an indispensable partner in our national response through evidence-based policymaking, technical assistance, resource mobilization, and global advocacy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "That partnership helped to mitigate an epidemic by means of one of the world's most successful national responses and placed Botswana firmly on the path towards ending HIV/AIDS as a public health threat by 2030."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Finance and jobs",
        "text": "Sought a stronger developing-country voice in financial governance, predictable concessional finance, blended investment, and funded technology-transfer and skills programs to address youth unemployment and climate-related needs.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "President, even as we work to restore trust, our world is transforming."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "Climate change is no longer tomorrow's warning."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "It is today's drought in Africa, floods in Asia, rising seas in the Pacific, and wildfires in Europe and the Americas."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "For Botswana, custodian of the Okavango Delta, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and the Kalahari ecosystem, climate change directly affects livelihoods, water security, and biodiversity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "Botswana remains committed to the 30 by 30 target and the sustainable management of our natural capital."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "President, Africa has the youngest population on Earth."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "That is an extraordinary asset if we invest in it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "But what is a demographic dividend today can become a demographic crisis tomorrow if opportunity does not keep pace with aspiration."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "Youth unemployment remains one of the most urgent challenges of our time."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "Managing it is a shared responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "Botswana calls upon the United Nations Development Programme, the International Labour Organization, and all relevant multilateral institutions to make technology transfer, skills development, and capacity-building funded priorities."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "As we will all agree, the credibility of our multilateral commitments will be properly tested in development finance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "When countries have the means to invest in their people, and when international institutions respond effectively to shared threats, trust is strengthened."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "But when commitments remain out of reach for those who need them most, confidence in the system weakens."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "Getting these fundamentals right is central to restoring trust, managing transformation, and building a United Nations that delivers for all."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "The global financial architecture must therefore evolve to reflect the economic realities of the 21st century, including financing demands created by climate change, technological transformation, and the imperative for sustainable development."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "Developing countries frequently face borrowing costs several times higher than those of wealthier nations because the system was not designed with the circumstances of the Global South in mind."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "Debt sustainability is a question of development and fairness."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "When nations spend more to service debt than to invest in education, job creation, or the provision of healthcare, trust in the system erodes."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "Botswana calls upon this Assembly and the international financial institutions to pursue reform of global financial governance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "This would give developing countries a meaningful voice and provide fair and predictable access to concessional finance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "We call upon the United Nations and its financial partners to mobilize private capital through innovative and blended financing agreements that de-risk productive investment in developing economies."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Technology",
        "text": "Supported an inclusive international framework for AI and emerging technologies, with developing countries helping set standards and safeguards rather than serving only as suppliers of critical resources.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "We also call on the United Nations to continue to explore the creation of an inclusive international framework on emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "We recognize technology as a bridge that narrows global inequality."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "This extends to critical minerals, rare earths, and energy resources that power the technological revolution, many of which come from developing countries."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "Therefore, developing countries must have a meaningful voice in setting the standards and safeguards that will govern these technologies, ensuring that they expand opportunities, support decent work, and strengthen public services while protecting human dignity, rights, and security."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
