  "CZE": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Ukraine and China",
        "text": "Condemned Russia’s war against Ukraine, urged higher costs for aggression alongside serious diplomacy, and called on China to use its influence to help end the war.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S017",
            "quote": "Instead, we should insist that with greater power comes greater responsibility: responsibility in the use of force, responsibility to exercise restraint, but also responsibility to use one’s influence to prevent force from becoming necessary in the first place."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S018",
            "quote": "This applies particularly to permanent members of the UN Security Council."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S019",
            "quote": "China has the power, influence, and responsibility to help prevent conflicts, de-escalate tensions, and contribute to ending wars."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "This includes using its influence to help bring Russia’s aggression against Ukraine to an end."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "That aggression was launched and continues to be waged by another permanent member of the UN Security Council, Russia, in violation of the UN Charter and fundamental principles of international law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "Russia’s aggression continues to inflict enormous suffering on the Ukrainian people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "Civilians and civilian infrastructure continue to be attacked indiscriminately."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "And the risks are growing day by day."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "Russia’s aggressive posture poses a direct threat to European security as a whole."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "The immediacy of that threat was starkly illustrated by the recent attempted Russian drone attack on Leipzig-Halle Airport in Germany, only 150 kilometers from the borders of the Czech Republic."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "The consequences of aggression reach far beyond Europe."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "Russia’s war has undermined global food security, disrupting agricultural production, exports, and supply chains."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "Its effects are felt in my country, but even more acutely in parts of Africa and elsewhere, particularly in countries that depend on stable and affordable food supplies."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "While we need to raise the costs of war for Russia, we must give serious diplomatic efforts a genuine chance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "Diplomacy matters most not between friends, but between adversaries."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "That is where the United Nations remains indispensable as a forum for dialogue, even when agreement seems very distant."
          }
