  "COD": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Conflict and diplomacy",
        "text": "Accused Rwanda of aggression through AFC/M23 and demanded implementation of Security Council resolution 2773. Welcomed U.S., Qatari, and AU diplomacy but sought deadlines, independent verification, and consequences for violations; said MONUSCO changes must depend on security conditions.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "President, few situations illustrate so painfully the gap between international commitments and lived reality as that of the east of the DRC."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "For more than three decades, millions of Congolese have been suffering attacks, forced displacement, and bereavement."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "Territories have been occupied, families dispersed, women and girls have suffered sexual violence, while children are recruited by armed groups or deprived of education."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "At the same time, the looting of our resources continues to fuel international trade."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "My country continues to face a war of aggression led by Rwanda through its proxy, the AFC/M23, in violation of its sovereignty, our sovereignty, and our territorial integrity, as documented by the UN."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "The atrocities committed by other armed groups, especially the ADF and CODECO, are exacerbating this humanitarian crisis even further."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "To combat this challenge, the DRC has chosen the path of diplomacy without ever abandoning its rights."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "The peace agreement signed in Washington on June 27, 2025, the commitments made as part of the Doha process, and the roadmap coordinated by the African Union have opened up prospects that we have constantly supported."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "I commend the United States, Qatar, the African Union, African facilitators, regional partners, and all those who are sincerely striving to restore peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "However, for the sake of truth, we must recognize that for millions of Congolese, this peace remains only a promise."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "Resolution 2773 of the Security Council has laid out an unambiguous path."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "It calls for an effective cessation of hostilities, the withdrawal of Rwandan forces from Congolese territory, an end to all support for armed groups, the disengagement of the AFC/M23, the dismantling of parallel administrations, the restoration of state authority, unhindered humanitarian access, and the safe and dignified return of displaced persons and refugees."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "But we do not need new texts to replace those that have already been adopted."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "What we need is their implementation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "With regard to the issue of the Democratic Liberation Forces of Rwanda, the FDLR, long cited by Kigali to justify its military presence in our territory, the DRC is shouldering its responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "The protocol signed by the political and military leadership of the FDLR on May 30, 2026, provides for the disarmament, demobilization, and containment of their combatants with a view toward their repatriation or resettlement, without prejudice to potential judicial prosecution for serious crimes, until the movement is disbanded."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "The repatriation on September 8, with the support of MONUSCO, of 120 persons associated with the FDLR is a first testament to the protocol's implementation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "The issue of the FDLR, therefore, should no longer serve as a pretext for maintaining a foreign military presence in our territory."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "The coordinated implementation of the mechanisms of Washington, Doha, and the African Union must be subject to a precise time frame, independent verification, regular information exchange, and clear consequences in case of violations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "In this context, MONUSCO maintains a vital role in protecting civilians, monitoring the ceasefire, and supporting agreed-upon mechanisms."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "Any change to its presence must be determined by the conditions of security on the ground, the strengthening of national capacity, and the guarantee that no vacuum of power will remain to the detriment of populations."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Domestic peace efforts",
        "text": "Reported steps toward FDLR disarmament and repatriation, security-sector reform, and national dialogue, while rejecting any framing of the conflict as solely an internal dispute.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "With regard to the issue of the Democratic Liberation Forces of Rwanda, the FDLR, long cited by Kigali to justify its military presence in our territory, the DRC is shouldering its responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "The protocol signed by the political and military leadership of the FDLR on May 30, 2026, provides for the disarmament, demobilization, and containment of their combatants with a view toward their repatriation or resettlement, without prejudice to potential judicial prosecution for serious crimes, until the movement is disbanded."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "The repatriation on September 8, with the support of MONUSCO, of 120 persons associated with the FDLR is a first testament to the protocol's implementation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "The issue of the FDLR, therefore, should no longer serve as a pretext for maintaining a foreign military presence in our territory."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "The coordinated implementation of the mechanisms of Washington, Doha, and the African Union must be subject to a precise time frame, independent verification, regular information exchange, and clear consequences in case of violations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "In this context, MONUSCO maintains a vital role in protecting civilians, monitoring the ceasefire, and supporting agreed-upon mechanisms."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "Any change to its presence must be determined by the conditions of security on the ground, the strengthening of national capacity, and the guarantee that no vacuum of power will remain to the detriment of populations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "The DRC, for its part, will continue to fully shoulder its responsibility, especially through pursuing reforms of its defense and security institutions, bolstering state authority, and reconstruction in territories affected by conflict."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "And because the peace sought in the sub-region ought to go hand in hand with cohesion within our nation, the President of the DRC launched on August 28 a national dialogue for peace, cohesion, and the rebuilding of the state."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "This dialogue is open to the political and social forces that are committed to the Republic, our Constitution, our territorial integrity, and the rejection of violence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "It does not aim to circumvent institutions nor to distribute power."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "It ought to help us address the structural causes of our vulnerabilities, consolidate national unity, and build a state that is more just, more involved, and more protective."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "Our hand remains outstretched toward all the children of Congo who choose peace, republican debate, and loyalty to their homeland."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "We Congolese speak to each other with frankness and responsibility, but no internal dialogue can transform an external aggression into a simple domestic dispute."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "At the same time, no external aggression should absolve us of correcting our own weaknesses."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "National cohesion and the defense of our territorial integrity are not mutually exclusive, but mutually complementary."
          }
