      {
        "label": "Minerals and industry",
        "text": "Proposed a UN-AU framework for fair, traceable critical-mineral value chains, local processing, and technology transfer. Sought elimination of child labor in mines and a Lobito Corridor that supports industrialization rather than raw-material exports alone.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "President, it is another paradox that my country's experience is showing the world: some of its resources that fuel conflicts on its territory are also those upon which a growing proportion of the transformation of the global economy depends."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "The governance of strategic resources ought to be an issue of peace, development, and global security from now on."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "The energy transition, the electrification of transport, energy storage, as well as the expansion of digital and AI infrastructure, are accelerating demand for copper, cobalt, lithium, nickel, and other critical minerals."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "As the largest global producer of cobalt and a major copper-producing power, the DRC is at the heart of this transformation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "Congolese cobalt is already being used in batteries, power grids, digital equipment, and technologies that are crucial for the decarbonization of the global economy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "It would be both unjust and dangerous for added value, jobs, know-how, and technologies to remain concentrated far away from the communities that are making these changes possible."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "We cannot build a decarbonized economy through bloodstained minerals, and we will not bring about a just transition by reproducing a greenwashed version of our past dependencies."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "The DRC therefore rejects the old model that limits producer countries to crude extraction while processing, research, technology, and the bulk of the profits are concentrated elsewhere."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "Our ambition is clear."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "We no longer wish to be simply the basement of the world's economy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "We plan to become a workshop, a laboratory, and a sovereign partner."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "We would like to further transform cobalt and copper, process more cobalt and copper on our territory, develop precursors for batteries and industrial components, train our engineers, support our researchers, and include our enterprises in global value chains."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "We would like to build, together with our African and international partners, competitive regional businesses that create jobs, skills, and shared prosperity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "This ambition, first and foremost, entails taking up our own responsibilities."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "The DRC is pursuing the modernization of mining governance through the transparency of contracts, extractive revenue, and beneficial ownership; improving mining registries; deploying traceability mechanisms; and fighting fraud."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "We are also accelerating the formalization of small-scale mining, the regulation of traders, the organization of cooperatives, and the securing of exploitation zones."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "The battle against child labor in mines, in this regard, is a moral and national obligation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "Together with the International Labour Organization, UNICEF, and our other partners, we are strengthening our identification, monitoring, and remediation mechanisms, as well as the training of our inspectors, children's school attendance, and economic solutions for their families."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "Our goal is unambiguous: we need to achieve zero children in the mines."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S094",
            "quote": "This responsibility lies with the Congolese state, but it also involves businesses, traders, refiners, manufacturers, financial institutions, and destination markets."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "The real proof of a responsible supply chain is not the electric vehicle sold downstream; it is the child who no longer descends into the mines upstream."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S096",
            "quote": "That is why the DRC proposes creating, under UN auspices and together with the African Union, as well as producer, processor, and consumer countries, a global framework for just, traceable, and resilient critical mineral value chains based upon the sovereignty of producer states."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S097",
            "quote": "It ought to guarantee the traceability of minerals, the responsibility of economic actors, the protection of workers and communities, as well as a more equitable sharing of added value thanks to local processing and technology transfer."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "The Lobito Corridor ought to become one of the tools to further this ambition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "We commend the commitment of Angola, Zambia, the USA, the European Union, the African Development Bank, financial institutions, and the private sector to promote its implementation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "The rehabilitation of railway links, the modernization of infrastructure, the facilitation of exchange, and energy investments can connect our territories, reduce logistical costs, and stimulate regional trade."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "The rehabilitation of railway links, the modernization of infrastructure, the facilitation of exchanges, and energy investments can connect our territories, reduce logistical costs, and stimulate regional trade."
          },
