          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "The Lobito Corridor ought to become a real backbone for regional industrialization, with the support of investors, with whom we hope to build transparent, sustainable, and mutually beneficial partnerships for the well-being of future generations."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Global governance",
        "text": "Supported two permanent African Security Council seats with veto rights while the veto exists, plus two additional elected seats. Backed the UN AI governance dialogue and a global capacity-building fund.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "Artificial intelligence today offers one of the most striking examples of this."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "It has immense potential, but also poses risks of new fractures."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "Its governance should not be the sole remit of certain powers or corporations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "Developing countries ought to be able to participate in defining its rules and to access the capacities that determine its use."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "The DRC supports the UN global dialogue on AI governance, as well as the creation of a global capacity-building fund."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "The digital divide must not become an intelligence divide."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "This need for inclusion ought first and foremost to be reflected in global governance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "Africa has proven itself over time to be a demographic, diplomatic, and geopolitical power, a vital one, but it still remains inadequately represented where decisions are being made about the world's future."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "How can we fail to mention the historic anomaly that is the absence of Africa among the permanent members of the Security Council?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "The admission of the African Union to the G20 is certainly a major step in the right direction."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "However, it is not sufficient to meet this need for representation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "As a member of the Security Council for 2026–2027, we reaffirm our support for the common African position enshrined in the Ezulwini Consensus and the Sirte Declaration, that is to say, two permanent seats for Africa with all of the associated privileges, including veto rights as long as they exist, and two additional non-permanent seats, in order to make the Council more representative, more legitimate, and ultimately more effective."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Development and resilience",
        "text": "Highlighted education, health coverage, and Ebola-response efforts; sought accessible climate finance, debt relief, and recovery of stolen assets, and proposed an African Coalition for Water Security.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "President, as you have understood, the transformation we are calling for at the UN is one we have chosen to launch first at home, convinced that by investing in our people, the main source of wealth of our nation, we will be paving the way toward renewed trust and lasting prosperity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "Since 2019, we have had free primary education, enabling more than 5 million additional children to attend school."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "In the 2023–2024 school year, more than 21 million children were enrolled in primary school, compared with 14.7 million four years earlier."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "This quantitative progress must now be transformed into quality."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "We are continuing to build and rehabilitate schools, and recently we have begun to roll out school cafeterias."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "Because access is not enough, every child must be able to learn in a school that is safe, inclusive, well-equipped, and open to the tools of our time."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S112",
            "quote": "This requirement applies especially to girls, children with disabilities, displaced children, and those whose schooling has been jeopardized by conflict."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S113",
            "quote": "The same ambition guides our health policy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S114",
            "quote": "We are continuing the gradual expansion of universal health coverage, in particular through free maternity care, improved maternal and newborn care, vaccination, access to essential medicines, the strengthening of the health care workforce, and expanded social protection."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S116",
            "quote": "President, every health crisis confirms the same truth: health sovereignty is built before emergencies."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S117",
            "quote": "It is based upon accessible health care systems, robust epidemiological surveillance, high-performing laboratories, well-funded research, and, above all, the trust of the population."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S118",
            "quote": "In this regard, the Ebola virus outbreak caused by the Bundibugyo strain remains a major test for our country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S119",
            "quote": "For the DRC, fighting this epidemic is an absolute priority."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S120",
            "quote": "After having contained 16 previous outbreaks, the DRC is mobilizing recognized scientific and operational expertise."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S121",
            "quote": "Thanks to national mobilization and the support of our partners, the response has recently begun producing tangible results."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S122",
            "quote": "In addition, clinical trials are now underway to evaluate vaccines and treatments for this strain in particular."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S123",
            "quote": "I would like to pay tribute to the Congolese and foreign health care workers, researchers, communities, and our partners, especially the WHO and the Africa Centres for Disease Control and Prevention, or Africa CDC, for their invaluable support to the DRC in eradicating this disease and strengthening resilience to it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S125",
            "quote": "President, this need for resilience does not stop at the boundaries of health."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S126",
            "quote": "It is also vital when it comes to climate disruptions, whose effects are already putting our societies under growing pressure."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S127",
            "quote": "Flooding, droughts, and erosion, not to mention population displacement, are threatening our stability."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S128",
            "quote": "In light of these upheavals, not all countries bear the same responsibility or the same burden."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S129",
            "quote": "Those who contribute least to global warming often suffer the heaviest consequences."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S130",
            "quote": "This paradox is all the more striking given that some of these countries are also among the main custodians of the natural assets upon which our common future depends."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S131",
            "quote": "The DRC is one of these custodians."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S132",
            "quote": "It is home to a vital part of the Congo Basin, which is one of the planet's greatest climate regulators."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S133",
            "quote": "Its forests, landscapes, freshwater, and biodiversity provide humanity with considerable ecosystem services."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S134",
            "quote": "This world heritage will continue to be preserved, but we maintain that the communities that protect it ought to be able to benefit from it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S135",
            "quote": "Climate finance, in this regard, is a fair solution."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S136",
            "quote": "However, it ought to be accessible, predictable, and proportionate to the services rendered."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S137",
            "quote": "Indeed, climate justice cannot consist in further indebting those who already bear the cost of damage they did the least to cause."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S138",
            "quote": "In the DRC, this ambition is taking shape especially through the Kivu-Kinshasa Green Corridor, which combines ecosystem preservation, economic development, and improved living conditions for the people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S139",
            "quote": "Generating 60 megawatts of electricity, this initiative also aims, by 2027, to create 25,000 jobs and protect 5,000 square kilometers of natural forest."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S140",
            "quote": "The climate crisis is also a water crisis."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S141",
            "quote": "Following the African Water Forum held in Djamena in July, the DRC has proposed the creation of an African Coalition for Water Security, which aims to strengthen regional cooperation and mobilize the financing needed to make water a driver of development and prevent tensions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S143",
            "quote": "President, these transformations require considerable resources."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S144",
            "quote": "Four years from the 2030 deadline, the Congolese roadmap for accelerating the SDGs estimates our needs at more than $70 billion."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S145",
            "quote": "We are strengthening our domestic revenue and enhancing the quality of public spending, but a country facing war, epidemics, poverty, and climate shocks simultaneously cannot close this gap alone."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S146",
            "quote": "At the same time, official development aid has fallen by more than 23% in real terms in 2025, which is the steepest annual contraction ever recorded."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S147",
            "quote": "This contraction undermines development efforts and jeopardizes the prevention of crises whose consequences go far beyond national borders."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S148",
            "quote": "ODA remains indispensable, but it will not be enough."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S149",
            "quote": "The Sevilla Commitment must now translate into better access to concessional financing, greater mobilization of multilateral development banks, and debt relief mechanisms that protect our state's ability to invest."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S150",
            "quote": "Lastly, no financial architecture can be sustainable without tax justice."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S151",
            "quote": "International cooperation must combat illicit financial flows, tax evasion, transfer pricing manipulation, and the laundering of revenue from natural resources."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S152",
            "quote": "Stolen assets must be rapidly identified, frozen, and returned."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S153",
            "quote": "Every penny recovered can fund a vaccine, a textbook, a well, or a road."
          }
        ]
      }
