  "DOM": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Haiti deadline",
        "text": "Called for renewal of the Gang Suppression Force before its stated 30 September expiry, full funding and troop deployment, enforcement of the arms embargo and sanctions, and stronger Haitian security and justice institutions.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, renewing peacekeeping operations, without a shadow of a doubt, is our most urgent task."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "Today, transnational criminal networks control territories, traffic arms and people, and recruit children."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "Haiti, our neighbor, is the clearest example of this."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "Since 2021, the Dominican Republic has warned in each and every forum that this crisis is a threat to the peace and security of the region, and particularly to my country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "A year ago, from this same rostrum, I called upon the Council to act without delay."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "Six days later, the Council adopted Resolution 2793, which authorized a Gang Suppression Force with a strong mandate and with the support of a United Nations support office."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "I thank the United States and Panama for their leadership, as well as Canada and other donors for their support; Kenya for its commitment; and all of the countries whose men and women are serving in Haiti today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "However, reality does not allow us to wait."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "One month ago, in the Haitian community of Kenscoff, in just one night, gangs murdered no fewer than 47 people, including five children."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "Close to a million and a half Haitians have been displaced from their homes."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "Half of them are children."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "This Assembly cannot resign itself to seeing massacres become the norm for the long-suffering Haitian people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "What the Council approved now requires the means to implement it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "First, the deployment of the force, which today is funded at only one fifth and has only one fifth of the authorized troops; second, fulfilling the arms embargo and sanctioning those who are financing and protecting gangs; and third, strengthening the police, the armed forces, and the Haitian justice system so that security can be sustained."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "The mandate of the force expires on the 30th of September."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "It is now for the Council to renew it and for the international community to contribute the troops and resources that are required."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "Renewing it without completing it would be prolonging an unfulfilled promise."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Contributions and borders",
        "text": "Thanked the United States, Panama, Canada, Kenya, and other contributors. Pledged financial, transit-logistics, sanctions, and medical support, while insisting that the Dominican Republic cannot substitute for a Haitian solution and will enforce its border and migration laws.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "I thank the United States and Panama for their leadership, as well as Canada and other donors for their support; Kenya for its commitment; and all of the countries whose men and women are serving in Haiti today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "However, reality does not allow us to wait."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "One month ago, in the Haitian community of Kenscoff, in just one night, gangs murdered no fewer than 47 people, including five children."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "Close to a million and a half Haitians have been displaced from their homes."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "Half of them are children."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "This Assembly cannot resign itself to seeing massacres become the norm for the long-suffering Haitian people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "What the Council approved now requires the means to implement it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "First, the deployment of the force, which today is funded at only one fifth and has only one fifth of the authorized troops; second, fulfilling the arms embargo and sanctioning those who are financing and protecting gangs; and third, strengthening the police, the armed forces, and the Haitian justice system so that security can be sustained."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "The mandate of the force expires on the 30th of September."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "It is now for the Council to renew it and for the international community to contribute the troops and resources that are required."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "Renewing it without completing it would be prolonging an unfulfilled promise."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "None of this requires a new decision."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "The Dominican Republic has played its role."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "We will not practice a diplomacy of mere declarations, but rather a diplomacy of solutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "We will contribute to building the consensus that made a resolution possible, and we are committing our financial contributions commensurate with the trust fund of the force, facilitating transit logistics from our country and the UN support office, cooperating with the sanctions regime, and supporting the personnel of the mission in our hospitals."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "We are doing this because this is, above all, a question of national security for our country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "And we must repeat this as clearly as possible: there is no Dominican solution to the Haitian crisis, and no state or organization can impose on our country the responsibility to do it in their place."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "We will continue to protect our borders, implement our migratory laws, and strengthen and equip our armed forces in the exercise of the sovereign equality that the United Nations recognizes for each state, fully respecting the international obligations that we freely assumed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "The solution to Haiti lies in Haiti itself."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "And the obligation of the international community is to make it possible, there in their country, for children to be able to go back to school and for Haitian youth to be able to have a future in their own country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "And, as soon as conditions allow it, for Haitians to be able to vote for the first time in a decade."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "UN leadership",
        "text": "Supported UN80 with adequate financing, a more representative Security Council, and a woman from Latin America and the Caribbean as the next Secretary-General.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S018",
            "quote": "President, for countries like ours, a rules-based order is a condition for our security and a guarantee that it is the norms agreed on by everyone, and not force, that resolve disputes between nations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S019",
            "quote": "It is for this reason that it is necessary to restore trust in this organization."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "And three things are necessary in this regard to achieve it: renewing representation, renewing peacekeeping operations, and renewing support for developing countries."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "We support the UN80 Initiative with conviction."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "However, no reform can be successful without resources behind it, and that is why the Dominican Republic is complying and playing a role."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "This year, we were one of the first countries to fully pay our contribution to the regular budget."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "Renewing representation requires a Security Council that looks more like the multipolar world of the present."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "And it also requires thinking about who will lead this organization next."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "This year, I affirmed from this very same rostrum that it was the turn of Latin America and the Caribbean to provide renewed leadership and that the time had come for a woman to be Secretary-General of this organization."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "The candidates who are running confirm this."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "In more than 80 years, no woman has led this organization."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "We trust that the Security Council and the General Assembly will rise to this moment."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Development and climate",
        "text": "Reported poverty reduction and investment gains. Sought development-finance criteria beyond GDP, faster climate finance, stable maritime entitlements amid sea-level rise, and stronger action on sargassum and ocean protection.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "President, the Dominican Republic has worked to fulfill the essential commitments to our people, and we have been able to show results."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "We have reduced monetary poverty by 25.8%, from 25.8% in 2019 to 14.6% in the first six months of this year."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "And just two months ago, the FAO confirmed that my country had been taken off the hunger map, becoming the fifth country in Latin America to achieve this."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "We committed to achieving the Zero Hunger goal by 2028, but we managed to achieve this before then."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "For four consecutive years, we have received more than $4 billion per year in foreign direct investment, and in 2025, for the first time, more than $5 billion."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "We are forecasting to receive more this year."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "Our exports reached a record of close to $16 billion."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "These results are a reflection of our legal certainty, institutional stability, and the trust that different actors have in the Dominican Republic."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "Peace, investment in new infrastructure, as well as the hospitality of our people, have led us to receive 7.5 million visitors in 2019, and this year we are predicted to exceed 12 million."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "This figure is only rivalled by Mexico in Latin America."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "However, progress in a country should not mean that a country is penalized."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "Middle-income countries host three in every four people on the planet and two in every three people in extreme poverty."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "Nevertheless, GDP continues to be used exclusively for concessional financing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "So, we are calling for a process like the one initiated in the Pact for the Future to achieve a common framework to measure progress beyond GDP, and for international financial institutions to incorporate these criteria in the multidimensional vulnerability index."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "Because what cannot be measured, what is not measured, does not influence decisions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "And what does not influence decisions does not receive attention."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "For a small island country, climate change is not an abstract matter, ladies and gentlemen."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "Our vulnerability is not a statistical category."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "It is the reality that we are experiencing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "And that is why we welcome that this Assembly has committed to adopting a declaration on sea level rise, guaranteeing stability in maritime areas."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "The declaration also includes sargassum, which is a scourge that afflicts the Caribbean coast every year, affecting tourism."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "Following an initiative by the Dominican Republic, the UN General Assembly and the Assembly for the Environment have adopted the first global resolution on sargassum, a regional problem recognized as a global challenge."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "We will not tire of calling for climate finance to be delivered as quickly as storms strike the Caribbean."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "In this vein, we have moved to ratify the BBNJ Agreement on biodiversity beyond national jurisdiction, and in March we deposited our instrument of ratification."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "The ocean is an important source of life and is our most extensive border, and that is why protecting it is a state obligation."
          }
        ]
      }
