  "ECU": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Organized-crime proposals",
        "text": "Proposed three UN-backed actions: a mechanism to trace and freeze illicit financial flows; a permanent information-sharing platform for police, prosecutors, and financial intelligence units; and inclusion of transnational organized crime in UN80 conflict-prevention priorities, with assistance to requesting states.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S010",
            "quote": "However, on this journey, we have learned something that I have come here to share with you: no state can defeat an enemy that knows no borders by acting alone."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S011",
            "quote": "The weapons that reach our streets cross several countries."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S012",
            "quote": "The money that finances mafias is laundered far from where the crimes are committed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S013",
            "quote": "The roots of drug trafficking, human trafficking, and illegal mining cross continents."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S014",
            "quote": "Criminals have already globalized their cooperation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S015",
            "quote": "They share routes, logistics, finances, and technology without red tape, distrust, or delay."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S016",
            "quote": "It is unacceptable that criminal organizations cooperate with one another more effectively than states do."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S017",
            "quote": "This is the reality that the United Nations must recognize and rise to."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S018",
            "quote": "For a long time, organized crime was dealt with as a law enforcement matter, but today we know that it is more than that."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S019",
            "quote": "When it controls territories and infiltrates institutions, replaces legitimate authority, erodes the rule of law, and destabilizes entire societies, and when that happens in several countries at the same time, it is no longer just a domestic issue; it becomes a threat to international peace and security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "I want to say this very clearly: we are not calling for other actors to act instead of states; we are calling for cooperation with full respect for the sovereignty of each nation and with results that we can measure."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "This is why Ecuador today is proposing three concrete actions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "First of all, an international mechanism within the framework of the UN to trace and freeze the illicit financial flows from transnational organized crime."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "Money is the fuel of these networks, so let us stop it in its tracks."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "Second, a permanent platform for information exchange between police forces, prosecutors’ offices, and financial intelligence units that enables states to anticipate rather than react once it has happened."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "The third concrete action is that the UN80 initiative include transnational organized crime as a priority for conflict prevention and provide the organization with the capacity to support states that request it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "These are proposals that Ecuador is prepared to support and drive forward alongside all countries that wish to join us."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Development finance and trade",
        "text": "Argued that security enables investment and poverty reduction. Sought financing eligibility based on vulnerability rather than income per capita alone and supported open, predictable, equitable trade.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "Excellencies, security is not an end in itself; it is a condition for a country to be able to flourish."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "Today, we are experiencing a crisis, a profound crisis, and recovering security means giving people hope for their future: for a young person to be able to choose university rather than being trapped by a criminal gang; for a family to open a business without fear; for a company to invest and create jobs; and for institutions to respond to the needs of citizens and not to illicit interests."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "Therefore, the success of an economy is not measured only by how much production grows, but rather by how much it is able to reduce poverty."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "It is measured in young people with decent jobs, children with a better education, and citizens who are able to build their future with dignity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "This must also guide the agenda of international development."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "Middle-income countries face vulnerabilities that income per capita does not reflect."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "We ask that access to cooperation and financing be defined using fairer vulnerability criteria and that the international financial architecture support the efforts of those who are undertaking reforms."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "We believe in open, predictable, and equitable trade."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "When a producer can export, innovate, and grow, there is a family behind them that can be lifted out of poverty."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "The best social policy is policy that generates opportunities."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Environmental security",
        "text": "Linked illegal fishing around the Galápagos and illegal mining in the Amazon to organized-crime financing, calling for international cooperation to protect natural resources.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "President, I come from a country that is small in size, but great, huge in terms of its nature."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "The Galápagos Islands, where Darwin found evidence of the evolution of life, are a World Heritage Site for the whole of humanity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "Today, they are threatened by illegal fishing networks that operate with the same logic and the same financing as other organized crime groups."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "The same is happening with illegal mining in the Amazon, which is destroying forests and funding gangs."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "Protecting nature is also a matter of security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "Ecuador will continue to fulfill its responsibilities and invites all of you to join us."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "AI and UN reform",
        "text": "Called for inclusive international AI governance that enables innovation and access for countries with fewer resources. Supported UN80 reforms focused on conflict prevention, operational capacity, and measurable results while respecting sovereignty and international law.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "One of the greatest challenges of the future is artificial intelligence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "It can transform education, multiply productivity, and close historic gaps, but also entrench inequalities and serve those that seek to weaken our institutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "We need international governance that enables us to innovate without renouncing our values and that does not leave those with the least resources behind."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "They also need to be able to access this technology."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "As Lin says, confidence in the multilateral system is going through difficult times."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "Many citizens see a gulf between what we agree on here and what people experience on a daily basis."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "Closing this gap is the task of our organization."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "A lot of citizens realize that this is the task that our generation must take up."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "As a founding country, Ecuador believes in the United Nations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "It is precisely for this reason that we want an organization that is able to respond to the challenges of the world today, not of 1945."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "Supporting the organization, the United Nations also needs a willingness to transform the United Nations, and that is why we support the UN80 initiative and pose an essential question: what United Nations does the world need today?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "We need an organization that is more efficient, with the ability to prevent conflicts, resolve crises, and support states facing challenges that did not exist when the organization was created."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "An organization whose legitimacy depends not only on the decisions that we adopt, but on the way that they are adopted."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "We need the Charter and international law to remain our common language."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "This remains our main strength."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "The citizens of the world will not judge this organization by its declarations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "They will judge it by its ability to turn commitments into peace and security, into respect for human rights, into real opportunities for development, and by how many lives we really save."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "President, the criminal gangs already coordinate with each other."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "Now we need to do better."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "Ecuador has come to this Assembly to defend collective solutions because no country can build a safe, prosperous, and sustainable future alone, and because, when international cooperation works, we are all stronger for it."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "issues": [
