  "EST": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Ukraine and accountability",
        "text": "Called for economic, diplomatic, and political pressure on Russia, accountability mechanisms, and support for Ukraine’s defense and recovery. Sought the return of transferred Ukrainian children and thanked Melania Trump’s humanitarian initiative. Said forces repeatedly cited for grave violations should not serve in UN peacekeeping.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen,One of the biggest tests for the UN's relevance is Russia's aggression against Ukraine."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "For more than 12 years, since the illegal annexation of Crimea and occupation of eastern Ukraine in 2014, a permanent member of the Security Council, the Russian Federation, has been perpetrating a war of aggression at the very heart of Europe."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "This aggression disregards the principles of the United Nations Charter to its very core."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "It violates respect for the sovereignty and territorial integrity of states and the prohibition on the use of force against another state."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "The consequences of Russia's aggression, however, extend beyond Ukraine and Europe."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "For example, by increasingly targeting Ukraine's Black Sea ports, commercial shipping, grain infrastructure, and alternative export routes, Russia is putting global food security at grave risk."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "As such, this is a concern for all of us, and rightly so."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "Russia's actions have been condemned by a large majority of this Assembly."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "But condemnation is not enough."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "We need to collectively force Russia into peace in Ukraine, to force it to the negotiating table by raising the cost of its aggression."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "For this, we can and should use the diverse instruments at our disposal, be they economic, diplomatic, or political."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "I strongly encourage more of my fellow heads of state and government to use this occasion to call on Russia to cease its aggression."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "Most of you have done so already, be it in the Global South or North."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "You have my appreciation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "The principles of the UN Charter cannot be trampled on."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "It is our collective task to stand up for them."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "We should also support the efforts of international mechanisms to document war crimes, ensure accountability, and provide assistance to those whose rights have been violated."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "Estonia is doing its part."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "We have completed all national procedures and taken the lead in discussions in Strasbourg to establish the special tribunal as soon as possible."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "A UN member state whose armed forces have been repeatedly cited in the UN Secretary-General's report for grave violations against children and conflict-related sexual violence should have no place in UN peacekeeping operations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "This is a matter of ensuring that perpetrators' actions have consequences."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "But it is equally a matter of maintaining trust in the integrity of UN peacekeeping."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "I fervently call on the UN to stop reflecting and instead take appropriate action immediately."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "Ukraine requires assistance in defending itself, but also in rebuilding the country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "Estonia, together with its partners, has worked closely to support Ukraine's cybersecurity and resilience in responding to evolving threats through the Tallinn Mechanism and the IT Coalition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "Estonia is also proud to be hosting the Ukraine Recovery Conference in 2027, organized in cooperation with our closest friends in the Nordic-Baltic region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "Building on the outcomes of earlier conferences, next year's event will advance, in practical terms, long-term international support for Ukraine and its recovery."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "As such, it will be a multilateral effort and an example of true cooperation for international peace and security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "One of the gravest aspects of Russia's war against Ukraine is the mass deportation and forced transfer of Ukrainian children, which is a systematic and deliberate attempt to erase their Ukrainian identity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S096",
            "quote": "It is a war crime and a crime against humanity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S097",
            "quote": "We therefore reiterate the call of the General Assembly resolution adopted on the 3rd of December 2025 and demand that the Russian Federation ensure the safe, immediate, and unconditional return of all forcibly transferred and deported Ukrainian children."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "We thank all of our international partners working to reunite these children with their families, in particular US First Lady Melania Trump, for a remarkable humanitarian initiative."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "UN decision-making",
        "text": "Supported UN80 and interoperable humanitarian data systems. Called for a woman Secretary-General, veto restraint in mass-atrocity cases, abstention by Council members party to a dispute, and stronger General Assembly action when the Council is blocked.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, if we want a United Nations that is more effective in terms of decision-making, more efficient in managing available resources, and up to date on technological developments, we should adopt as our shared task the readjustment of the structure of the United Nations around the three pillars, as well as reassessing how the United Nations operates."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "Estonia supports system-wide reform of UN80 and the humanitarian reset, which are both well underway and have already delivered some encouraging results."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "Now it is time to build on this momentum and move decisively forward with reforms."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "We need ambition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "For example, the humanitarian sector, alongside stronger data harmonization, could move towards a shared interoperability model that allows many systems to coexist while quickly and safely exchanging data."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "Estonian humanitarian organizations are already testing these solutions, from Palestine to Sudan."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "We also need determination."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "Above all, we need action, action that strengthens the UN as a main actor responsible for multilateral cooperation and prepares it for future challenges."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "This year, the United Nations is set to make arguably one of its most consequential decisions: the selection and appointment of its next Secretary-General."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "As an active member of the Accountability, Coherence and Transparency Group, Estonia has stood for a transparent, fair, and inclusive process."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "At this challenging time for the organization, we need a strong and principled leader with an impeccable track record in championing and upholding international law, human rights, and the principles of the Charter."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "Estonia also feels that, after 81 years, it is time for the organization to be led by a woman."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "Allow me to take this opportunity to commend and express our gratitude to our current Secretary-General, Mr."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "António Guterres, for his steadfast commitment to the principles of the UN Charter, including his support for a just and lasting peace in Ukraine."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "With regard to the Security Council, it must be said that its inability to take timely and decisive decisions on some of the worst crises we are seeing today risks rendering the United Nations irrelevant."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "We have not seen unified and decisive Council action on Ukraine, Sudan, or Myanmar."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "The use of the veto and the threat of its use continue to loom over the Council and paralyze any of its attempts to take action."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "Estonia has strongly advocated for permanent members to refrain from vetoing resolutions aimed at ending mass atrocities, in line with the France-Mexico proposal and the ACT Code of Conduct."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "It is also important to call on the Security Council members to start fully implementing Article 27.3 of the Charter once again and to abstain in cases where members of the Council are a party to a dispute."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "The General Assembly resolution, Uniting for Peace, gives the most representative and democratic body of the United Nations a toolbox to act on matters related to international peace and security when the Council is unable to deliver."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "In concert, we must reinforce the role of the General Assembly when it comes to peace and security, and this will help us collectively find solutions where the Council is powerless."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Gaza and regional security",
        "text": "Reaffirmed support for UNRWA, humanitarian access, and a negotiated two-state solution. Condemned Iran’s attacks on Gulf states and supported freedom of navigation and a coordinated response to the instrumentalization of migration.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "My fellow leaders, while the situation in Ukraine and Ukraine's security have affected Estonia most directly, we are neither indifferent to nor unaffected by the impact of other wars, threats, and conflicts."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "The situation in the West Bank and Gaza remains of great concern."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "Innocent civilians and children must not bear the devastating human cost of the war."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "Estonia has consistently called for upholding international humanitarian law and ensuring safe, rapid, and unhindered access to humanitarian aid for those in need."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "We remain a stable donor to UNRWA and are committed to a credible political process leading to a negotiated two-state solution, with Israel and Palestine living side by side in peace, security, and dignity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "We have provided food aid to hospitals in Gaza and stand ready to offer our digital transition expertise in its future reconstruction."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "Estonia has consistently condemned the attack by Iran against our close partners, the Gulf States, and has shown its readiness to contribute to ensuring freedom of navigation in the region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "This is an issue that affects us all."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "We also see the instrumentalization of migration as a means of exerting pressure on countries, whether on the European Union's eastern and southern borders or elsewhere."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "Irregular migration is increasingly becoming a security issue, and it requires a coordinated international response."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "AI and human rights",
        "text": "Highlighted its AI-governance dialogue co-chair role with El Salvador, AI-supported education through UNICEF, and an ITU Development Bureau candidacy. Reaffirmed women’s rights, sexual and reproductive health and rights, and work with Colombia and New Zealand on maternal mortality.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, Estonia firmly believes that respect for human rights is a prerequisite for peace, security, and prosperity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "We stand firmly behind the United Nations human rights system and will continue to defend and strengthen it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "As one of the first supporters of a Global Alliance for Human Rights, Estonia feels that human rights should once again be at the center of the world we choose to build."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "Estonia is a member of the United Nations Human Rights Council for the period from 2026 to 2028 and is currently serving as vice president of the Council."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "As a country ranked among the world's top three for press freedom, we are committed to promoting media freedom, protecting journalists, and enhancing media literacy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "We will continue our strong commitment to women's rights and gender equality, including sexual and reproductive health and rights."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "Together with New Zealand and Colombia, Estonia is leading negotiations at the Human Rights Council on the resolution on preventing maternal mortality and morbidity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "Maternal survival is a question of justice and human rights, not only health care."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, artificial intelligence is here to stay and to be used to assist us, as has been the case with every major technology throughout human history."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "Like any new technology, AI poses risks and brings challenges."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "But with knowledge, wisdom, and unity, we can put it to use in the service of humanity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "As co-chair of the first UN Global Dialogue on AI Governance, alongside El Salvador, Estonia has proudly brought its knowledge and experience in service of the UN and its member states."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "Personally, I had the honour to become one of the commissioners of the AI for Good Global Commission this summer."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "For me, this role means both trust and responsibility to help ensure that AI serves people, that its use is secure and reliable, and that its benefits reach as many countries and communities as possible."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "As current president of the UNICEF Executive Board, Estonia has been paying particular attention to the topic of innovation in education, notably how to advance safe, inclusive, and child-centered learning in a responsible way with the support of AI."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "In Estonia, we have introduced a massive education innovation program we call the AI Leap, whose aim is to assist schools, students, and teachers alike to adapt to the age of AI and foster meaningful learning."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "Artificial intelligence should empower teaching and learning rather than replace them."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "Under the auspices of the United Nations, notably through close cooperation with UNICEF, we are bringing our experience and best practices to the global scene, ensuring that AI creates equal opportunities for all humanity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "We know for certain that digitalization, which has now been reinforced by AI, has enabled our small country to grow, innovate, and connect globally."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "This is why we have shared our experience with around 150 other countries worldwide."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "And this is also why Estonia has nominated a candidate for the position of Director of the ITU Development Bureau."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S112",
            "quote": "You can trust us to work to turn connectivity into lasting capability and to ensure that no country is left behind in the digital transformation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S113",
            "quote": "We hope to count on your valuable support."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
