  "ETH": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Maritime access and regional security",
        "text": "Said reliable access to the sea is essential to Ethiopia’s sustained development and that it is pursuing diplomatic avenues to secure it. Supported a Sudanese-led, Sudanese-owned peace process and regional cooperation in the Horn of Africa.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "President, Ethiopia has diligently worked to promote cooperation and regional integration through infrastructure development, trade, and people-to-people relationships in the Horn of Africa."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "We have achieved notable progress with several of our neighbors, in spite of attempts by reckless external actors who are habitually engaged in fomenting instability."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "Despite continued interference in our internal affairs by adversarial elements, we have exercised immense restraint and remained guided by the firm conviction of becoming one of the most prosperous and dynamic development engines in Africa."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "Our message to forces of destruction and mayhem is loud and clear."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "We urge them to respect the sacred right of the people of the Horn of Africa to live in peace and prosperity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "Turning to the wider region, Ethiopia has consistently supported efforts by subregional and regional organizations to bring durable and lasting peace in Sudan."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "We firmly believe that a peaceful resolution can only be achieved through a Sudanese-led and Sudanese-owned peace process that reflects the true will and aspirations of the Sudanese people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "To sustain and scale up the success we have achieved in renewable energy, connectivity, food security, manufacturing, and urban development, Ethiopia calls for genuine and sustained regional and international cooperation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "Despite these tremendous achievements, Mr."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "President, we have come to recognize that our efforts to build a strong economy cannot generate sustained development without reliable and dependable access to the sea."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "We believe that maritime access can be managed for the common benefit and progress of all countries in the region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "It is upon this unwavering aspiration that we are pursuing all possible diplomatic avenues to secure access to and from the sea to ensure Ethiopia’s integration into the global trading system."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "UN reform",
        "text": "Called for comprehensive Security Council reform to provide Africa equal representation, grounding its position in sovereign equality and Ethiopia’s experience with collective security.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S007",
            "quote": "Sixty-three years ago, in 1963, Emperor Haile Selassie famously cautioned this global community by stating, “Lasting peace can be achieved only when nations recognize that their true strength lies not in the domination of others, but in cooperation anchored upon a genuine equality.” As a founding member of the United Nations, Ethiopia bears the scars of historical betrayal and the unyielding conviction of a survivor."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S008",
            "quote": "When the League of Nations abandoned our appeal against fascist aggression in the 1930s, we did not surrender to despair and desolation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S009",
            "quote": "We resolutely stood firm as champions of collective security, helping give birth to the very organization in which we stand."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S010",
            "quote": "Today, we call upon the community of nations to summon that same foundational courage to actively reinforce the very ideals that help prevent global conflict and the scourge of war."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S011",
            "quote": "The question, therefore, is: how much longer shall we wait before the pillars of collective security fracture beyond repair?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S012",
            "quote": "This is exactly what drives the significance of multilateralism, not as a diplomatic convenience, but as a living shield rooted in sovereign equality to address the shifting tides of power politics."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "President, Ethiopia remains steadfast in its belief that the United Nations must be fundamentally reformed to best address shifting global challenges."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "UN reform must reflect our highest aspiration to witness an organization anchored in true equality and justice."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "Africa has waited for too long in the shadow of global decision-making."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "Now it is demanding immediate justice through the comprehensive reform of the United Nations Security Council."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "With genuine political goodwill, how can a world with the right conscience justify the denial of 1.6 billion Africans the right to equal representation?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "That indeed is a generational quest for truth and morality."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Climate and connectivity",
        "text": "Invited leaders to COP32, which the speech said Ethiopia would host in November 2027. Highlighted tree planting, food security, renewable energy, the Grand Ethiopian Renaissance Dam, and transport infrastructure, seeking sustained international cooperation.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "Poverty and systemic inequality also fuel ecological and environmental crises."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "Excessive consumption by the few drives the emissions that are currently choking our planet."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "Yet, delayed promises take a brutal toll in the loss of lives and the devastation of infrastructure."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "If we are to survive this crisis, we must act now and act fast."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "Speaking of action, my country, Ethiopia, will proudly host COP32 in November 2027."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "Ethiopia will help organize a vibrant and inclusive platform for the private sector and international stakeholders to pioneer tangible solutions to climate action."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "In this connection, I sincerely invite all world leaders to come to Ethiopia and leave their footprints at this important global climate summit."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "A significant leap has also been achieved in attaining food security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "As part of fulfilling our commitment to enhance resilience to climate shocks, we were able to produce an improved climate-resilient wheat variety seed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "In a very short period, we have transitioned from a wheat importer to one of the largest wheat producers in Africa."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "At a time when food provision has become a political battleground and the global food supply hangs precariously in the balance, we send a clear message that Africa can feed itself."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "Since the launch of the Green Legacy Initiative in 2019, we have been able to plant 56 billion trees, which is not only expanding our forest coverage but also significantly restoring our ecosystem."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "At this stage, this initiative is expected to sequester approximately 1.22 billion metric tons of carbon dioxide annually."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "As one of the powerhouses of clean energy, with a total potential of 60,000 megawatts, Ethiopia targets generating 13,000 megawatts by 2030, aiming also to scale up our energy supply across the East African Power Pool and beyond."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "In this regard, the Grand Ethiopian Renaissance Dam stands as a monumental Pan-African clean energy project, proving that our shared waters and resources can generate progress and development for collective regional prosperity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "Moreover, adding to Ethiopia’s growing portfolio of mega-project execution, the government is investing in an international airport worth $12.5 billion, which will handle 110 million passengers and about 4 million tons of cargo annually."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "This project will play a catalytic role in the African Continental Free Trade Area."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "To sustain and scale up the success we have achieved in renewable energy, connectivity, food security, manufacturing, and urban development, Ethiopia calls for genuine and sustained regional and international cooperation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "AI and national development",
        "text": "Called for the Global South to help lead the AI transition rather than remain a recipient of technology. Cited the 5 Million Coders Program and a planned AI university, alongside reported progress in elections and national dialogue.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "With regard to the digital revolution and artificial intelligence, Africa is compelled to ask a defining question: will the age of AI become another instrument of global inequality, or will it be a catalyst for our collective growth?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "We must ensure that the Global South leads this technological revolution rather than remain a helpless spectator."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "Nevertheless, some of the initiatives we see from the Global South give a beacon of hope that we can indeed attain technological advancement through foresight and leadership."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "A case in point is Ethiopia’s initiative of the 5 Million Coders Program and the soon-to-be-commissioned University of Artificial Intelligence, which reaffirm that our continent is ready to build the future."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "President, Ethiopia will continue its commitment to the realization of our overarching goal of building a democratic and prosperous country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "The progress we have achieved so far in various facets of development reflects this firm and strong resolve."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "We recently held a democratic election that laid a strong foundation for a free, fair, and transparent political dispensation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "Equally, in our relentless pursuit of building national consensus, the National Dialogue Commission has convened the first historic summit, where citizens from every corner of the country and from all walks of life deliberate on critical issues of national importance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "It has now opened a glorious new chapter in our political history that helps strengthen our democratic institutions."
          }
        ]
      }
