  "GIN": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Governance and sovereignty",
        "text": "Argued that governance models should reflect national historical, social, and cultural conditions rather than be externally imposed. Sought mutually beneficial partnerships respecting sovereignty while reaffirming international law and the UN Charter.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S010",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, three years ago, from this rostrum, I spoke with the candor to which my country and our continent are bound."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S011",
            "quote": "I spoke the truth, and I stated that the model of imported governance, without being adapted to our continent, was not generating the fruits that had been expected by our peoples."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S012",
            "quote": "This is something which I stand by."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S013",
            "quote": "But today, I am once again speaking before you with a different mindset."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S014",
            "quote": "I do not seek to denounce, but rather to share with you factual elements about the progress and headway that have been made by the Republic of Guinea, as we have achieved results that have emanated from the choices that we have made."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, heads of state and government, our recent experience permits me respectfully to state a certainty: when governance models are tailored to reflect the historical, social, and cultural realities of each nation, rather than haphazardly being imposed, that is when development accelerates."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "Let us consider Asia."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "Let us consider certain nations in the Middle East."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "They did not wait for an external model to be endorsed in order to become prosperous."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "They drew inspiration from universal experience, while at the same time tailoring that to their national brilliance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "In one generation, they managed to achieve what others spent a century attaining."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "Africa too can embark upon this path."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "This is not reflective of a rejection of the world, nor a rejection of international cooperation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "Quite to the contrary, this is a call for win-win partnership, a partnership that is respectful of the sovereignty of each nation, rooted in win-win collaboration rather than pre-established arrangements which disregard our realities."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "The Republic of Guinea, for our part, is and shall remain a reliable, open, and engaged partner vis-à-vis the international community, while engaging in mutual respect for the sovereignty of one and all."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "President, Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen, the Republic of Guinea is advancing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "We are making headway by harnessing our own means, by capitalizing upon our own choices for the benefit of our own people, and we are doing so in a manner that is in accordance with international law, with the spirit of the Charter of the United Nations, and in the spirit of candid and inclusive cooperation with all of our partners."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "I cherish the hope that this Guinean experience can, to a modest degree, stimulate more in-depth consideration of the manifold legitimate development pathways for our continent."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Political transition",
        "text": "Reported completion of presidential, legislative, and communal elections and establishment of domestically financed institutions. Presented the constitutional framework as supporting local representation, peaceful transfers of power, and cultural and religious plurality.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S015",
            "quote": "On the basis of our Constitution, the Republic of Guinea organized entirely direct presidential, legislative, and communal elections, and we have established all institutions, which are entirely financed by our treasury."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S016",
            "quote": "I state this with a rightful sense of pride: none of these elections, which were held throughout our territory, were marred by any significant incidents on the part of any of the participants in this electoral process."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S017",
            "quote": "This reflects the fact, ladies and gentlemen, that a country can independently organize, using its own resources, credible, peaceful, and transparent elections."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S018",
            "quote": "This Constitution that we have adopted introduces profound innovations in terms of peaceful coexistence, as well as greater representation of our localities and communities, novel guarantees for the peaceful transfer of power, and recognition of our cultural, linguistic, religious, and cultural plurality as the bedrock of our nation and not as a divisive factor."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S019",
            "quote": "This I state with a sense of legitimate pride."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "All of these elections were organized on our soil, once again, without any assistance from any party whatsoever."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Economic transformation",
        "text": "Reported new roads, schools, hospitals, completion of the Simandou mining and infrastructure project, an operational gold refinery, and three aluminum refineries under construction. Described Simandou 2040 as a broader infrastructure, agriculture, energy, education, and health program.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, I did not come here to engage in rhetoric, but I do believe it is worthwhile to share with you a simple overview and useful information about what the Republic of Guinea has achieved in less than three years."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "We have paved more than a thousand kilometers of roads, which have connected our regions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "We have the Simandou mega-project, Africa's largest mining and infrastructure project, which is currently complete."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "We have schools and hospitals that have been built throughout the Republic of Guinea."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "We have three aluminum refineries under construction, as we seek to transform our bauxite on our own soil."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "We have Africa's largest gold refinery, which is currently operational and has already been completed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "We have a sustainable and responsible socioeconomic development program for my country for the next 15 years, which I refer to as the Simandou 2040 project."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "The Simandou 2040 program embodies a transformation initiative for our economy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "This is not merely a mining project."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "This represents a meaningful strategic lever to accelerate the development of infrastructure, agriculture, energy, education, and health, to name just a few."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "These are results that we have achieved in less than three years."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Youth opportunities",
        "text": "Prioritized education, labor-market-oriented training through the Simandou Academy, employment, and entrepreneurship as the basis for national development.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "Our most valuable asset remains our youth, and we must provide them with high-quality education, training opportunities that reflect the needs of the labor market through the Simandou Academy initiative, as well as meaningful opportunities for employment and entrepreneurship."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
