  "HND": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Investment and legal certainty",
        "text": "Invited investment under predictable rules, respect for private property, and treaty compliance. Reported adherence to IMF guidelines and a March 2026 return to the investment-arbitration framework identified in the transcript as CIADI.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "Honduras exercises sovereignty over the full extent of its national territory."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "Moreover, it administers its natural resources in accordance with its Constitution."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "The law applies to each and every individual in all four corners of the country because, without legal security and certainty, and without respect for private property, there can be no peace, development, employment, or investment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "The right to development is something that the country's government has a duty to ensure for the millions of Honduran people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "Honduras makes good on its promises; it honours its agreements and treaties."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "These principles are neither selective nor biased."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "Honduras is a conscientious country, a country of law, a country in which we invite you to invest."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "Anyone who invests in Honduras will be offered opportunities, order, transparency, and clear rules."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "We are adhering to International Monetary Fund guidelines."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "In the seven months that my country has been in office, we have increased our international reserves by $1.3 billion, an increase of 13%."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "We returned to the International Centre of Arbitration, CIADI, on 6 March 2026."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "We had been members of that centre since 1989, and we returned to resolve our problems with a sense of solemn responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "With these steps, we sought to reiterate that, in Honduras, rules apply to everyone and rules are followed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "On that basis, Honduras can offer concrete investment opportunities in logistics, industry, energy, infrastructure, agro-industry, mining, tourism, to name just a few sectors."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Security and Ukraine",
        "text": "Supported Ukraine’s territorial integrity and political independence. Called for coordinated action by like-minded democracies against transnational criminal networks, alongside stronger Honduran police and armed forces.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "I visited Ukraine three months ago."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "There, I saw a people defending their freedom and fighting for it, in full respect of their territorial integrity and political independence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "I saw a country protecting civilians and working to achieve a lasting peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "Security cannot be imposed by decree."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "It is something that is built with resources, training, and political resolve."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "Today, that is exactly what we are doing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "We are equipping and strengthening our national police force and our armed forces."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "We are doing this because transnational organized crime does not respect borders."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "Drug trafficking networks and gangs operate in several countries at the same time, and no country can vanquish them alone."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "It is a matter of shared responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "Every nation must do its part."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "Democracies whose interests are aligned must unite and act together quickly and with resolve."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "It is only in so doing that we will enjoy security and prosperity in our hemisphere."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Infrastructure and jobs",
        "text": "Promoted Puerto Cortés, an Atlantic–Pacific logistics corridor, energy-sector investment, manufacturing, agriculture, mining, and tourism. Sought investment that remains in the country, creates jobs, and transfers skills to young people.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "On that basis, Honduras can offer concrete investment opportunities in logistics, industry, energy, infrastructure, agro-industry, mining, tourism, to name just a few sectors."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "We are the centre of America."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "We stand between two oceans."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "We are optimizing Puerto Cortés, a port on our Caribbean Atlantic coast."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "It is the port with the greatest potential for growth in the country and one of the largest and most important ports in Central America."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "We are investing to strengthen our road infrastructure so that we can create a logistics corridor linking the Atlantic with the Pacific."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "This project and its location mean that we can offer the world safe, reliable, and efficient supply chains."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "Honduras is one of the world's key textile exporters."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "We manufacture the clothes of well-known brands."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "We also manufacture cable harnesses and automobile parts that are sold around the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "They come from Honduran factories."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "Around 200,000 Honduran people work in those industries."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "These factories, maquilas, and other forms of industry require stable energy at competitive prices."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "It is for that reason that the National Congress recently adopted a reform to our electrical energy law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "That reform had been championed by the presidency."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "In light of the above, we invite both national and foreign investment: investment in the development of Honduras's energy sector, and investment in the generation, transmission, and distribution of energy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "Our land is fertile."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "We are the largest coffee exporter in Central America and the fifth largest globally."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "Fifty-seven percent of the coffee that Honduras exports is recognized as extremely high-quality, accredited, and specialized coffee, reflecting the quality of our production and its standard of excellence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "Honduras sees its agriculture, fisheries, and poultry industries as fundamental pillars for economic development, food security, and job creation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "Our commitment is to breathe momentum into these sectors sustainably."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "We want to empower our producers and bring high-quality Honduran products to international markets."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "Our land harbours mineral wealth with vast potential that has yet to be harnessed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "We have the opportunity to develop a modern, responsible, and sustainable mining industry so that we can create employment and transform these resources into development and prosperity for our people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "We want to develop these resources with clear rules, in full respect for the environment and for the benefit of our communities."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "Our extraordinary biodiversity, natural riches, and cultural heritage make us a country with a vast wealth of potential for tourism."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "We have crystal-clear waters and reefs in the Bay Islands."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "We have the great Copán ruins and the legacy of the Mayan civilization."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "All of these things mean that we offer the world a unique combination of nature, history, and culture."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "Above all, we have the most valuable asset that any nation can hold: a young, hardworking, and capable population, a population that demands, and quite rightly so, the opportunity to use its talent in its own country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "We want to see investment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "We want investment to arrive in the country and to stay."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "We want investment that creates jobs and brings knowledge to the table to train our young people."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Public services and resilience",
        "text": "Said spending reductions were intended to support health, education, infrastructure, and security while preserving fiscal stability. Requested partners for water, agriculture, early-warning systems, and climate-resilient infrastructure amid a severe drought.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S014",
            "quote": "President, since the very first day in office, we decided to govern differently, with deeds."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S015",
            "quote": "We are reducing expenditure so that we can invest in healthcare, education, infrastructure, and security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S016",
            "quote": "We are doing all of that while guaranteeing macroeconomic stability and a great deal of fiscal responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "President, there is another challenge that no country can face alone: natural phenomena."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "Today, we are weathering a severe drought, and we are taking tangible decisions to support our most vulnerable citizens."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "The hurricanes that have beset us in the past and today's drought have the same root cause: a climate that is operating at increasingly extreme levels and that will affect the entire world for decades."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "Our response is not simply to react to these disasters."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "Rather, we are taking action by preparing as best we can to mitigate the effects of climate change."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "We are investing our own resources in protecting lives, harvests, and access to drinking water."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "However, we want to go further."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "Honduras is opening its doors to anyone developing new solutions for water, agriculture, early warning, and the infrastructure that our country requires."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
