  "IRN": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Response to the United States",
        "text": "Rejected President Trump’s terrorism characterization and accused the United States and Israel of attacks on Iranian leaders, civilians, and infrastructure. Portrayed Iran’s military actions as defensive and denied targeting civilian populations; these are the speaker’s claims.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S004",
            "quote": "Secretary-General, Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen, I had prepared a speech to present to you yesterday."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S005",
            "quote": "The United States President described us as terrorists."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S006",
            "quote": "We have been the victims of terrorism."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S007",
            "quote": "I come from an Iran in which our esteemed Supreme Leader was assassinated without any legal framework or reason."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S008",
            "quote": "I come from an Iran where, in truth, they bombed a school."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S009",
            "quote": "You see these children?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S010",
            "quote": "These children perished under bombs, with weapons used by the United States and Israel."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S011",
            "quote": "They were innocent and had committed no crimes."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S012",
            "quote": "Lamerd, one of the small cities in a province in Iran, had a sports hall where children were busy playing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S013",
            "quote": "The United States, by using weapons with multiple warheads, targeted that sports hall."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S014",
            "quote": "They martyred and assassinated our scientists, our men, women, and children."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S015",
            "quote": "Innocent children who, in truth, had committed no crimes, no sins."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S016",
            "quote": "Those who are terrorists and train and protect terrorists describe us as such."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S017",
            "quote": "We have only defended ourselves."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S018",
            "quote": "We are not terrorists."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S019",
            "quote": "Our innocent people have been the targets of cowardly attacks and aggressions imposed upon our country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "And we defended ourselves with utmost strength."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "America and Israel attacked us equipped with the latest technology and weapon systems, and our people stood steadfast."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "Yes, they did hit us, but we did not bend the knee."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "We did not bow our heads."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "We responded, but we did not hit civilian populations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "They came into surrounding territories and targeted our universities, our healthcare centers, our schools, our hospitals, our infrastructure, all of it against international law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "We need strength because a people who are unable to defend themselves will be trampled upon in today’s world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "We live in a world in which the powerful, instead of thinking about humanity, justice, fairness, and democracy, seem to be the protectors and creators of instability and destruction."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "Whomever they wish to discredit, they label as terrorists."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "For the past two centuries, Iran has not attacked any country or territory, but we have always defended ourselves steadfastly."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "But now we are being accused of being a source of instability in the region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "We are labeled terrorists."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "And this has made it so that the path that we have chosen for ourselves requires power to defend ourselves."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "We do not seek power in order to attack or commit aggression."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "We seek energy for progress, not to threaten societies with weapons."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "And we wish to cooperate and collaborate for security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "The people of Iran, in the past seven months, have been in the streets every night demonstrating in support of their land, of their homeland, so as not to allow those who were equipped, trained, and armed by Israel and America to disrupt the security of their country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "For seven months, day and night, they have been present in the streets."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "They are our source of power and our support, and that is why we stand fast."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "Iran must be powerful so as to avoid being threatened, to avoid its future being threatened."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "We do not wish to use our power for hegemony, and we do not seek our security in the insecurity of others."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "Vis-à-vis Iran’s defense, our defensive systems have been built so that no one can think that the bombing of Iranian cities will go unanswered."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "That is why we have the military power we do: for defense."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "But we say it clearly: in order to defend our country, we do not seek anyone’s permission or approval."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Nuclear position",
        "text": "Rejected nuclear weapons while insisting on unrestricted access to peaceful nuclear technology for medicine, agriculture, industry, and energy. Criticized what he described as unequal treatment of Iran and Israel in inspections and sanctions.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "We seek energy for progress."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "For years, they have labeled centrifuges, international sanctions, and other matters when it comes to our nuclear technology."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "But for our country, peaceful nuclear technology is part of our inherent progress."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "For our sick people, it is cure and treatment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "For the agricultural sector, it is food security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "For industry, it is advancement and progress and the supply of electrical energy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "Iran does not accept nuclear technology being at the exclusive disposal of some, of a handful."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "We will not bow our heads and give up the right that is inherently ours."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "We say it clearly: no nuclear weapons and no limitations to peaceful nuclear technology."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "Our peace will not come in the field of battle, but they must give the needed security to the people and nation of Iran."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, the topic of this gathering is mutual trust."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "That cannot be achieved through words only, but by abstaining from using double standards."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "Atomic and nuclear bombs are in the hands of the Israeli regime, but inspectors are requested to come to Iran."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "Israel has savagely murdered over 70,000 innocents in Gaza, but Iran, while at the table of negotiation, was bombed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "Israel has the bombs, has weapons of mass destruction, is not a member of the Non-Proliferation Treaty, and during her shameful life has not allowed a single inspection, but they are rewarded by all the means necessary for them to be able to bomb any capital in the region at will."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "I will repeat: the nuclear weapon is in Israel, but the inspectors are in Iran."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "Israel kills, but Iran is subject to sanctions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "This is a true tragedy, which would make anyone hearing it laugh at best."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "They kill, we are sanctioned, we are punished."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "Those who are ill, innocent people, the poor, and the least privileged in our society are the targets of these sanctions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "And this is what the United States seeks to do with all countries: to sacrifice the population of a country in order to achieve her illegitimate goals."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "If we seek true peace and stability, we must apply a single standard for all."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "Iran does not seek special treatment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "We seek equal rights."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S112",
            "quote": "We assume the responsibility, accept the responsibility that comes with it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Regional security",
        "text": "Called for regional states to resolve regional problems without outside interference. Said security around the Strait of Hormuz must be shared and opposed use of the waterway to facilitate attacks on Iran or deny Iranian access.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "We seek cooperation in order to have security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "We live in a region in which warfare knows no borders."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "Crisis in one land will spill into the surrounding nations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "That is why Iran does not see her neighbors as security rivals."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "We want to have strong neighbors in the waters of the Strait of Hormuz."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "We cannot let some have free access and gain their interests from a waterway while, at the same time, using that waterway to impose their aggressions upon us, to impose insecurity upon us, to forbid us access to our own waterways."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "They close access for us to our own waterway, yet they keep supplying missiles and deadly military technologies to bring insecurity to all of the lands surrounding that waterway."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "We will not succumb to that."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "The expansion of warfare will not result in security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "One cannot create chaos for the coastal countries seeking naval security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "Our regional issues must be resolved in the region, at the hands of the countries in the region, without becoming a toy in the hands of outside aggressors."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "No relationship with a foreign power can become a tool for threatening neighboring countries in the region."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Palestine and diplomacy",
        "text": "Accused Israel of genocide in Gaza and argued that resistance would continue while occupation and injustice persisted. Said Iran remained ready for dialogue and negotiations but would not accept coercion or surrender its stated rights.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "In Gaza, over 80,000 innocent civilians have been brutally murdered."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "Hundreds of thousands have been displaced."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "They are committing genocide by using the so-called technologies that they have at their disposal."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "Excellencies, vis-à-vis Palestine, Palestine remains an open wound on the conscience of the international community, and Gaza remains a symbol of the failure of international mechanisms to prevent civilian suffering."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "For decades, resolutions have been adopted, yet occupation and violence have continued."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "We cannot speak of peace while ignoring Palestine."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "Lasting peace in West Asia is impossible without justice for Palestine."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "As long as occupation, aggression, and injustice persist in the world, resistance will continue."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "If it is weakened in one form, it will reemerge in others, perhaps stronger still."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "Gaza, despite relentless killing and widespread devastation, has strengthened the people’s faith in resistance, and resistance cannot be destroyed by bombs and siege."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "This is human nature."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "If a human being is driven from his or her land, they will resist."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "If their homes are subjected to bombings, aggression, and attacks, they will resist."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "What other choice do they have?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "Succumb to bullying, be driven from their homes and their lands, and remain silent in the face of these threats and dangers?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "And when they defend themselves, they are labeled as terrorists?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S118",
            "quote": "Iran extends her hand towards the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S119",
            "quote": "We invite the world, we call on the world, not out of weakness, but out of a deep belief in our own power and steadfastness, to cooperate and collaborate because of a deep belief that no one in this region will have security alone."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S120",
            "quote": "Either we will build it together, or we will have to live under insecurity together."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S121",
            "quote": "We seek to think about a worthy future in which security, fairness, justice, and human dignity will become unalienable rights for all people, for all humans."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S122",
            "quote": "A future in which no people are driven to the sidelines, no voice is lost in the chaos of power, and no power will have the right to determine the future of a people other than those people themselves."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S123",
            "quote": "If we truly seek to have an order based on international law and standards, it must be based on justice, common human will, and uplifting human dignity, because a peace that does not encompass all is no peace, and fairness and justice that do not embrace all are not worthy of being called justice and fairness."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S124",
            "quote": "But going back to the words of the President of the United States yesterday shows those who are experts in international law, dialogue, diplomacy, and basic human standards that everything uttered about our country goes against the very essence, charter, and spirit of the United Nations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S125",
            "quote": "He must know that the resistance of the Iranian people will only increase in the face of sanctions, increased pressure, and increased bullying."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S126",
            "quote": "We will never bow our heads or bend at the knee."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S127",
            "quote": "Iran must be understood by Mr."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S128",
            "quote": "Trump and those who seek to bully us: we are ready for dialogue, diplomacy, and negotiations without accepting the language of force."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
