      {
        "label": "AI and UN reform",
        "text": "Called for UN-led common AI rules balancing transparency, oversight, security, intellectual-property protection, and human control without excessive bureaucracy. Sought a more representative and accountable Security Council and reiterated support for a universal death-penalty moratorium and women’s rights.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "We stand at the dawn of a technological revolution that is already reshaping the way we live, the way we work, produce, and make decisions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "It is the artificial intelligence revolution."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "The great inventions of the past took centuries to transform the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "Artificial intelligence is doing so in a matter of years."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "Those who control these technologies will enjoy an enormous advantage over those who are left behind."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S094",
            "quote": "The risk is that new inequalities, new dependencies, and new concentrations of power, or even new forms of domination, will emerge."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "Entire professions may disappear or be transformed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S096",
            "quote": "Falsifying and manipulating reality will become ever easier."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S097",
            "quote": "Automated systems operating without human oversight may produce extremely dangerous decisions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "Pope Leo XIV, in the encyclical Magnifica Humanitas, reminded us that no algorithm can take the place of human conscience and that any technology capable of striking without seeing the face of another person lowers the moral threshold for conflict."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "Italy shares this vision."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "But governing innovation does not mean demonizing it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "Artificial intelligence can open up possibilities that today are unimaginable in medicine, for example, research, education, manufacturing, and environmental protection."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "Every major technological advance has generated fears, but has also created opportunities and, over time, greater prosperity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "Turning back is neither possible nor desirable, but neither can we hand over our future to technology without rules."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "We do not need bureaucratic cages that can only be respected by some."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "We need a balance between transparency, oversight, security, and the protection of intellectual property."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "We need to share the benefits of innovation and build mechanisms of mutual oversight."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "This is precisely the task of the United Nations: to establish common rules before events or the strongest actors impose their own."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "The United Nations was founded in 1945 out of a world in ruins, a world that had learned a simple truth: when each of us stands alone, we all lose."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "Eighty-one years later, that lesson is more relevant than ever."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "The United Nations was created to prevent violence from becoming the only law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "But to remain faithful to that mission, it must regain its ability to make decisions and, above all, to act."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S112",
            "quote": "With this conviction, Italy will continue to advocate for a universal moratorium on the death penalty, a cause rooted in civilization, in the defense of life and human dignity, which we have championed for years here in this very building."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S113",
            "quote": "We are also on the front line in defending individual freedom and women's rights, and fighting, among other things, the abhorrent practice of female genital mutilation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S114",
            "quote": "We must have the courage to say it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S115",
            "quote": "Too often, this organization appears powerless."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S116",
            "quote": "For far too long, its reform has been held back by competing interests."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S117",
            "quote": "Italy wants a Security Council that is more legitimate, more representative, and more accountable to all member states."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S118",
            "quote": "Not a more exclusive club, but one of the pillars of the far-reaching renewal of the United Nations that we hope the new Secretary-General will want to pursue, making it capable of deciding and acting while there is still time to change the course of events."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Africa and migration",
        "text": "Presented the Mattei Plan and IMEC as partnership mechanisms. Linked African investment, vaccine production, education, and jobs to stability; supported agreements with origin and transit countries against trafficking and irregular migration alongside safe, regular pathways.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "Dialogue, however, is not a sign of weakness, nor does it mean neutrality."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "Italy knows where it stands."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "Our home is Europe."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "Our alliance is with the West, and our values are freedom, democracy, and the dignity of every human being."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "Yet belonging to the West does not mean retreating behind fortress walls."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "It requires us to draw on the strength of our values to engage with others, build partnerships among equals, and mend the fabric of an international system that risks descending into chaos."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "The European Union, the G7, and the West, of which we are proud to be part, must not be perceived as walls."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "They must be bridges."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "This is the purpose of IMEC, the economic logistics corridor designed to connect Europe with the broader Indo-Mediterranean region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "The same principle guides our relationship with Africa, a strategic priority for Italy and a major partner for our century."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "The Mattei Plan now involves 18 countries and is built on a simple idea: not to decide for Africa, but to decide with Africa."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "It is not aid handed down from above, but a partnership among equals in agriculture and energy, education and training, infrastructure, and the pharmaceutical sector."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "Producing vaccines in Africa saves lives, strengthens health systems, creates jobs, and supports growth capable of generating stability."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "It is in this spirit, and in defense of the right not to be forced to migrate, that we fight against human traffickers who prey on poverty."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "Agreements with countries of origin and transit help us combat irregular migration, while education, training, and access to employment support safe and regular migration."
          }
        ]
      }
