  "KEN": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Security Council reform",
        "text": "Called for equitable permanent representation for Africa and other underrepresented regions, with all privileges of permanent membership. Argued that selective application of international law and unequal decision-making undermine trust in collective security.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "On peace and security, the contradiction is increasingly difficult to ignore."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "Every nation in this hall has one vote."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "Every nation is sovereign and equal under the Charter."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "Yet, on the gravest question of war and peace, five nations possess a permanent power that the other 188 do not."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "The equality proclaimed in this Assembly ends at the doors of the Security Council."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "That imbalance might have reflected the world of 1945."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "It does not reflect the world that we know today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "Africa has 54 member states, more than a quarter of this Assembly, yet no permanent voice in the body entrusted with the primary responsibility of international peace and security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "We are frequently the subject of its decisions, permanently discussed, yet permanently excluded."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "The problem is not that the world lacks law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "It is that confidence in its consistent application is weakening."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "International law cannot be invoked loudly in one crisis, cautiously in another crisis, and disregarded when convenient."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "Every perceived double standard carries a price, and that price is trust."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "Trust cannot be restored by declaration."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "It must be earned by consistent application."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "But the cost of failure is measured in more than lost trust."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "It is measured in children driven from their classrooms, children who go to sleep hungry, children who learn the sound of gunfire before they know the safety of peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "When collective security breaks down, schools close, hospitals collapse, families flee, and economies are consumed by war."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "Peace is not separate from development."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "It is its first condition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "When the institutions entrusted with peace fail, it is too often the youngest who inherit the consequences."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "Excellencies, Africa exposes this contradiction most clearly."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "In 1945, most of our continent could not speak for itself at San Francisco because it remained under colonial rule."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "Only four African states were represented."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "The architecture of collective security was therefore designed at a moment when most Africans had neither a nation at the table nor a voice in shaping the institutions that would govern peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "The world, ladies and gentlemen, has since transformed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "The Council, the Security Council, has not."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "We cannot manage transformation with institutions that refuse to transform themselves."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S158",
            "quote": "Whether in the Security Council or in the international financial system, institutions built for another age are being asked to govern a completely different world from the one we live in today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S159",
            "quote": "Restoring trust requires more than defending those institutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S160",
            "quote": "It requires having the courage to reform them."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S161",
            "quote": "This is not a conversation we are beginning today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S162",
            "quote": "For decades, member states have debated how to make the Security Council more representative, legitimate, and effective."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S163",
            "quote": "In 2008, after years of discussion, this General Assembly moved Security Council reform into intergovernmental negotiations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S164",
            "quote": "Those negotiations began the following year."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S165",
            "quote": "Seventeen years later, we are still negotiating."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S166",
            "quote": "The central questions remain before us: membership, the veto, regional representation, the size and working methods of the Security Council, and its relationship with this General Assembly."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S167",
            "quote": "The world has not stood still while we have been debating these issues."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S168",
            "quote": "In the Pact for the Future, member states agreed that redressing the historical injustice against Africa must be a priority in Security Council reform."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S169",
            "quote": "In the Pact for the Future, Member States agreed that redressing the historical injustice against Africa must be a priority in Security Council reform."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S170",
            "quote": "We should not accept that reform is impossible because it is difficult."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S171",
            "quote": "This organization has changed its architecture before."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S172",
            "quote": "In 1963, this General Assembly adopted amendments to enlarge the Security Council."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S173",
            "quote": "The Council grew from 11 members to 15 because Member States recognized that the institution had to respond to a changing membership."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S174",
            "quote": "What was possible then, ladies and gentlemen, is possible today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S175",
            "quote": "Reform must deliver equitable and permanent representation, with all the prerogatives and privileges of permanent membership, to Africa and other deserving regions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S176",
            "quote": "Political reform and financial reform are not separate projects."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S177",
            "quote": "They ask the same fundamental question: whether the institutions that govern our common future will reflect the sovereign equality they proclaim or preserve inequalities inherited from another age."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Financial architecture",
        "text": "Sought fairer sovereign credit assessments, more and longer multilateral-development-bank lending, guarantees and risk sharing, and long-term local-currency finance. Requested greater African influence in financial institutions while acknowledging governments’ responsibilities for debt management, contracts, and anticorruption.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "But national effort can only go so far when the international financial system makes development more expensive."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "The countries that most need capital frequently pay the highest price to obtain it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "Developing countries have recently borrowed at rates two to four times higher, on average, than developed nations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "The question, therefore, is not simply whether finance is available."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "It is who can access it, at what price, for how long, and under whose assessment of risk."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "Africa knows the cost of that assessment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "Sovereign credit ratings shape perceptions of risk, the interest countries pay, and even the volume of finance available to them."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "UNDP estimates that subjectivities in credit ratings have cost African countries approximately $75 billion through excessive interest and foregone lending."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "Risk, ladies and gentlemen, must be measured, but it must also be measured fairly."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "We cannot build a fair global economy if the nations with the greatest development needs face the highest cost of development finance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "A road that is commercially viable should not become unviable merely because it crosses an African border."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "A power project should not cost more simply because of the passport of the country in which it is being built."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S112",
            "quote": "Capital must price risk."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S113",
            "quote": "It must not price prejudice."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S114",
            "quote": "Reform of the international financial architecture must therefore begin with the cost and availability of capital."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S115",
            "quote": "The UN Charter envisaged multilateral development banks that lend more, lend longer, and mobilize private capital at scale."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S116",
            "quote": "It further contemplated guarantees and risk-sharing instruments that reduce the cost of viable investments."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S117",
            "quote": "And we need greater access to long-term and local currency finance so that countries are not forced to build long-term infrastructure with short-term, expensive money."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S118",
            "quote": "And by the way, this is not an argument against responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S119",
            "quote": "Governments must also do their part to manage debt prudently, strengthen institutions, prepare pipelines of credible projects, deepen domestic capital markets, honor contracts, and confront corruption without equivocation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S120",
            "quote": "A fairer international system requires responsibility on both sides."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S121",
            "quote": "Reform abroad cannot substitute for accountability at home."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S145",
            "quote": "The imbalance is not only about money."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S146",
            "quote": "It is also about voice."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S147",
            "quote": "Africa's 54 nations are home to nearly one in every five people on earth."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S148",
            "quote": "Yet our influence on the institutions that govern global finance remains disproportionately small."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S149",
            "quote": "We cannot carry substantial obligations under a system while remaining marginal in shaping its rules."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S150",
            "quote": "If Africa has a stake in the burden of debt, Africa must have a share in the decisions on how that debt is acquired."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S151",
            "quote": "This is not a plea for special treatment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S152",
            "quote": "It is a proposition for shared prosperity."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Industrialization and investment",
        "text": "Urged local processing of African resources and use of AfCFTA to build industrial value chains. Announced an expected groundbreaking the following week for an East African refinery in Lamu and sought both foreign investment and mobilization of African institutional capital.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S122",
            "quote": "Distinguished delegates, Africa does not come to plead."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S123",
            "quote": "We come with a proposal."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S124",
            "quote": "Our continent holds vast mineral wealth, immense agricultural potential, extraordinary renewable energy resources, and the world's youngest population."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S125",
            "quote": "We are a market of more than 1.5 billion people, increasingly connected through the African Continental Free Trade Area."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S126",
            "quote": "These are not merely African assets."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S127",
            "quote": "Properly developed, they are part of the answer to the world's search for food security, clean energy, resilient supply chains, and a new source of growth."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S128",
            "quote": "Africa's resources must become the beginning of African industry, not the end of Africa's contribution to the value chain."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S129",
            "quote": "Extraction defined too much of our past."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S130",
            "quote": "Investment must underpin our future."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S131",
            "quote": "This transition is already taking shape."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S132",
            "quote": "Cocoa-producing nations are moving from bean to brand."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S133",
            "quote": "Cotton producers are building garment value chains."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S134",
            "quote": "And Africa has made its position clear."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S135",
            "quote": "The clean energy transition must not become another extractive transition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S136",
            "quote": "The African Continental Free Trade Area must be more than a market for what Africa already produces."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S137",
            "quote": "It must become the platform on which Africa makes more of what it now imports."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S138",
            "quote": "Kenya intends to be part of that transformation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S139",
            "quote": "In the next week, we expect to break ground on the East African refinery in Lamu, a refinery capable of producing 700,000 barrels of oil a day, an investment of approximately $16 billion."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S140",
            "quote": "Its significance extends beyond one project or one country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S141",
            "quote": "It represents the Africa we seek to build, adding value at home, creating jobs for our people, and building industries capable of serving continents and global markets."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S142",
            "quote": "That transformation should be financed using foreign and domestic resources."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S143",
            "quote": "And that is what we intend to do, including the more than $4 trillion in domestic capital across pension funds, insurance assets, sovereign wealth funds, banks, and other institutions in Africa."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S144",
            "quote": "The task is to mobilize more of that capital for productive investment while building the safeguards, credible projects, and financial instruments that long-term investors require."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Education and development",
        "text": "Linked debt-service burdens and conflict to reduced spending on schools and health. Highlighted Kenya’s reported investments in teachers, classrooms, laboratories, and higher education as part of its national development strategy.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "But the cost of failure is measured in more than lost trust."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "It is measured in children driven from their classrooms, children who go to sleep hungry, children who learn the sound of gunfire before they know the safety of peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "When collective security breaks down, schools close, hospitals collapse, families flee, and economies are consumed by war."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "Peace is not separate from development."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "It is its first condition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "When the institutions entrusted with peace fail, it is too often the youngest who inherit the consequences."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "The test of equality does not end with the institutions that govern peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "It extends to the institutions that shape prosperity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "The same question confronts us there."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "Does the international financial system give every nation a fair opportunity to secure the well-being of its citizens?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "The Charter did not conceive development as charity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "It pledged social progress, better standards of life, and economic and social advancement for all people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "Yet, for too many countries, the resources required to fulfill that promise are being consumed before they can reach their people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "Global public debt reached a record $102 trillion in 2024."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "Developing countries accounted for less than a third of that debt, yet paid about a trillion dollars in interest on debt in that year alone."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "Put differently, 46 developing countries now spend more on interest on debt than on classrooms and medicine."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "Behind these numbers lies a simple reality."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "The hospital competes with a creditor."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "The classroom competes with debt service."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "And too often, the creditor, debt service, is paid first."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "And it is our children who inherit the consequences."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "Today, 251 million children and young people remain out of school."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "Millions more enter classrooms without the teachers, books, meals, and facilities they need to learn."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S094",
            "quote": "When debt service displaces investment in education, we are not merely balancing budgets."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "We are transferring the cost of today's financial burden to the next generation of citizens."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S096",
            "quote": "Kenya has chosen to invest in the next generation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S097",
            "quote": "Over the last four years, we have spent an additional $5.3 billion in education, recruited 100,000 additional teachers, built more than 23,000 new classrooms, and are developing another 1,600 laboratories while expanding support for universities and technical institutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "We do this because education is not consumption."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "It is the infrastructure of opportunity, productivity, and national transformation that supports global advancement."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
