  "LBY": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "National political process",
        "text": "Called for constitutional and legal mechanisms, referendums, and free elections to end division. Insisted on national ownership, equal participation, rejection of force, and transparent implementation with timelines and oversight; welcomed UNSMIL facilitation without external custodianship.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, after years of political division and polarization that have drained the state and society, Libya no longer needs more crisis management, but rather the will to end the crisis."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "Our goal is clear: a unified, sovereign state whose institutions derive their legitimacy from the will of its people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "The path to that goal is a return to the people through constitutional and legal mechanisms, referendums, and free and fair elections."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "The people are the source of legitimacy, and it is they who can give institutions their unity and stability."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "Temporary deals cannot do so, nor can fragile settlements that collapse whenever the balance of power shifts or loyalties change."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "We welcome the effort and intention of every state sincerely seeking to end the political and institutional division."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "We also appreciate the role entrusted to the United Nations Support Mission in Libya and its responsibility for facilitating the political process."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "Nevertheless, past experience obliges us to be clear."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "Any sustainable political process must not violate four governing principles."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "First, respect for legitimacy and for the constitutional and legal frameworks in force, without circumventing them or creating political arrangements outside established frameworks and procedures."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "Second, the principle of national ownership is a red line."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "International mediation must not turn into custodianship or into solutions crafted from abroad."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "The will of Libyans is the foundation, and the inclusion of all the different parties without exclusion or imposition is the true guarantee of the sustainability of any solution."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "Third, ensuring equal opportunities for all parties, as well as rejecting the use of force, influence, or a fait accompli to impose predetermined political outcomes."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "Fourth, commitment to transparency in understandings and agreements."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "This requires defining the phases of implementation, their timelines, and the entities responsible for them."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "It also requires establishing clear mechanisms for oversight and accountability, so as to ensure outcomes that are implementable, legally sound, and capable of producing legitimate and stable institutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S094",
            "quote": "Experience has taught us that fragile settlements can begin to unravel as soon as the balance of power shifts or their outcomes emerge."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "Any arrangements that disregard national legal frameworks expose themselves to challenge and dispute."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S096",
            "quote": "They reproduce the crisis rather than end it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S097",
            "quote": "Sustainable legitimacy and legality are not created by a fait accompli, nor are they protected by shifting balances of power."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "They are created by the will of the people and protected by the law."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "New committee and accountability",
        "text": "Announced a national de-escalation and confidence-building committee and requested UN and partner support. Urged the Security Council to act on Panel of Experts findings and apply relevant sanctions without selective enforcement.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "In this context, we call upon the Security Council to discharge its responsibilities and to follow up on the United Nations reports submitted to it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "This includes the report of the Panel of Experts on Violations and Cases of Non-Compliance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "We call upon the Council to give serious consideration to the Panel's recommendations and to take the necessary action within its established mandates."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "The purpose is to ensure the effective implementation of the Council's resolutions and the relevant sanctions measures without selectivity or double standards."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "Documented violations should not become mere recurring facts in reports."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "Nor should accountability end at documentation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "The authority of international law and the credibility of institutions are measured by their ability to move from monitoring violations to holding perpetrators accountable, and from resolution to implementation for all without exception."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "In translating these principles into national responsibility and concrete action, we announce from this rostrum the launch of work on a national committee for de-escalation and confidence-building."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "The committee will draw on national and local initiatives."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "It will aim to prevent conflicts, contain escalation, and prevent its recurrence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "This is in addition to supporting reconciliation and creating a safe environment for the political and electoral process."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "Here, we call upon all Libyan parties to engage in this framework."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "We also call upon the UN and Libya's partners to support and facilitate it with full respect for sovereignty and national ownership."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Regional diplomacy",
        "text": "Supported Palestinian statehood and expressed solidarity with Saudi Arabia. Linked Sudan and Sahel instability to Libya’s security, while seeking Mediterranean partnerships in development, trade, energy, and investment beyond migration management.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S009",
            "quote": "That reality unfolds before us at every moment in Palestine, whose delegation, we regret, has not been able to participate with us in this session."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S010",
            "quote": "There, the plight of the Palestinian people continues to worsen after decades of occupation, repression, and the alteration of their identity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S011",
            "quote": "Yet, they remain steadfast in their adherence to their right to life and to self-determination."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S012",
            "quote": "These are rights guaranteed without discrimination by international law and international humanitarian law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S013",
            "quote": "All of humanity yearns for international instruments and resolutions to move from texts and promises to reality, and for the right of the Palestinian people to their state to be realized in accordance with international law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S014",
            "quote": "The continued undermining of these prospects for its establishment not only squanders opportunities for peace, but also drives the region towards a cycle of conflict, the spread of extremism, and the search for alternatives amid major expansionist projects that extend beyond occupied Palestine to Syria and Lebanon."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S015",
            "quote": "Neither the Islamic and Christian holy sites nor civilians and civilian infrastructure in Palestine have been spared the ravages of this conflict."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S016",
            "quote": "Its repercussions have extended to the Arabian Gulf, most recently in the attack against the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S017",
            "quote": "We affirm our full solidarity with the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia in safeguarding its security, its territorial integrity, its citizens, and its holy sites."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S018",
            "quote": "We reject any targeting that threatens it or endangers Islamic holy sites."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S019",
            "quote": "The security of the Kingdom and the Gulf, given their Arab and Islamic weight, is not a national matter, but a pillar of the security and stability of our region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "The ongoing armed conflict in Sudan, our brotherly neighbor, has made its people the victims of a devastating war for which they are paying a hefty price."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "In that war, interests and interventions collide, and its effects extend beyond the borders of Sudan, endangering the security and stability of the region and the unity of its states."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "The instability in the Sahel region represents an existential threat to the integrity of states."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "That threat stems from the nexus of terrorism, organized crime, poverty, climate change, displacement, and migration, and from the widening cycle of armed conflict in the region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "It is no longer acceptable for the world to regard the Sahel merely as a source of resources, an arena for international competition, or a footnote in global decision-making."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "Africa, whose journey we have followed since the founding of the African Union, is not the margin of the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "It is one of the centers of the world to come."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "Libya does not lie on the edge of Africa."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "Libya is of Africa, of its history, of its security, and of its future."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "Decades ago, an African will emerged from the Libyan city of Sirte that contributed to the establishment of the African Union."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "That fact reminds us that Libya has never been merely a bridge between Africa and the Mediterranean, but a partner in shaping the African project itself."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "We therefore view the security of the Sahel region as part of Libya's own security and stability."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "We view the security and stability of the states of the region and all our African neighbors, near and far, together with developing Africa, as an investment in the common security of Africa and its European neighborhood."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "This is not assistance provided by one party to another, nor is it a responsibility borne by one party alone."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "Likewise, we view the Mediterranean basin not as a barrier between Africa and Europe, but as a shared space for connection."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "Relations among its countries should move beyond merely managing migration and crises towards making the Mediterranean a bridge for development, trade, energy transition, investment, and common security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "We want strong relations with our Arab surroundings, especially our neighboring countries."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "We want Libya to regain its natural role within its African continent."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "We want balanced strategic partnerships with our Mediterranean neighbors and our regional and international sphere based on a single principle: namely, common interests, mutual respect, non-interference, and respect for national sovereignty."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "Libya's true ally is not one who seeks out the strongest party within it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "The true ally is one who wants a strong Libyan state."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "The true partner is not one whose interests are tied to the continuation of division."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "The true partner is one whose shared interest with us grows as Libya becomes more united, stable, and prosperous."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "We want states to compete in Libya on investment, reconstruction, energy, technology, and development, not for influence within its institutions."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Council candidacy",
        "text": "Announced Libya’s bid for an African Security Council seat for 2028–2029 and sought member-state support, presenting a unified Libyan state as a partner for regional security and cooperation.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "Ladies and gentlemen, a Libya that regains its sovereignty and the unity of its institutions will not be a gain for Libyans alone."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "It will be a force for stability in the Arab world, a source of strategic depth for security and development in Africa, a responsible partner in the Mediterranean, and a bridge for cooperation between North and South."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "From this rostrum, Libya announces its candidacy for membership of the Security Council for the term 2028-2029 for the African seat."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "Its campaign is conducted under the slogan, “Consolidating Justice for Security and Peace: Libya, a Bridge Among Nations.” Libya looks forward to the confidence and support of the member states in this endeavor."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "This candidacy is not merely a diplomatic ambition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "It embodies a national will for Libya to regain its natural role in the international arena and to shoulder its responsibility for the maintenance of international peace and security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "It stems from a firm conviction that peace is built not merely on the absence of conflict, but on establishing justice and addressing the causes of injustice and instability."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S112",
            "quote": "Libya does not seek a seat merely to occupy a position; rather, it seeks to contribute to building a more equitable international order and to serve as a bridge among nations, a voice for consensus, and an active partner in peacemaking."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S113",
            "quote": "Hence, our message to our friends and partners is not that they should abandon their interest in Libya, but that they should build those interests with us on a firmer foundation: namely, that their interests lie in Libya's stability, not in the fragility of institutions, and in partnership with Libya, not in influence within it."
          }
        ]
      }
