      {
        "label": "Ukraine and Middle East",
        "text": "Supported Ukraine and diplomatic efforts toward a just peace. Called for civilian protection and aid access in Gaza, a two-state solution, Hamas disarmament, and freedom of navigation through the Strait of Hormuz.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "Excellencies, Montenegro remains committed to supporting Ukraine and welcomes all credible diplomatic efforts aimed at bringing the war to an end."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "We believe that a just and lasting peace must be achieved through dialogue and diplomacy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "In Gaza, our responsibility begins with the protection of human lives."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "Civilians must be protected, and humanitarian assistance must reach those in need safely and without obstruction."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "Israelis deserve lasting security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "Palestinians deserve dignity, freedom, and a viable state of their own."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "Montenegro supports a two-state solution, with the State of Israel and a viable State of Palestine living side by side in peace, security, and mutual recognition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "The disarmament of Hamas remains an important element of a sustainable settlement, while full respect for international humanitarian law must guide us throughout."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "Different conflicts have different histories."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "But human dignity cannot have different standards."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "Neither can international law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "The same commitment to international law applies to freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz, a route whose security has implications far beyond the region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "Disruptions affect energy markets and global trade, but they also affect food security through the supply and price of fertilizers and other critical agricultural inputs, with particularly serious consequences for vulnerable import-dependent countries."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "UN reform",
        "text": "Supported a more effective, accessible, and financially sustainable UN and a more representative, transparent, and accountable Security Council, emphasizing responsibility when the veto affects responses to mass atrocities.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "This commitment comes at a time when the United Nations itself is facing a profound test."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "Eight decades after its foundation, the challenges confronting this organization are increasingly complex and interconnected."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "Conflicts are eroding trust in the international system."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "Climate change is testing the resilience of states and societies, and artificial intelligence and other emerging technologies are creating risks at a speed that national frameworks alone cannot adequately address."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "So, the answer cannot be less multilateralism."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "It must be more effective multilateralism."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "Montenegro, therefore, strongly supports the UN reform agenda and the ambition to build a United Nations that is more effective, more agile, more accessible, more financially sustainable, and fit for the challenges of our time."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "This reform must strengthen the UN's ability to deliver where it matters most: in preventing conflict, protecting human rights and freedoms, advancing sustainable development, and responding effectively to humanitarian crises."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "This responsibility also extends to the Security Council itself, which must become more effective, representative, accountable, and transparent."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "The exercise of the veto must carry the weight of conscience."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "Above all, when the world is confronted with mass atrocities and the large-scale loss of civilian life, the Charter of the United Nations must remain our common reference point."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "Montenegro will be a constructive partner in those efforts."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Rights and future generations",
        "text": "Advocated protections for independent institutions, media, and civil society; meaningful youth influence in decisions; human-centered, rights-based AI; and climate cooperation attentive to countries with low emissions but high exposure.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "Dear colleagues, human rights are at the heart of the society we are building at home and of the international order we promote abroad."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "Human dignity is universal and indivisible."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "That means protecting the rights and freedoms of every single person, combating discrimination and hate speech, and safeguarding the independent institutions, free media, and civil society on which our democratic societies depend."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "Montenegro is proud of its multi-ethnic, multi-religious, and multicultural character."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "We understand that diversity is not a challenge to be managed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "It is a strength to be protected."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "Montenegro sits where the Mediterranean Sea meets the Balkans."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "We are a small country shaped by different cultures, religions, and identities."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "Our history has taught us that living together cannot be taken for granted."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "It has to be renewed by every generation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "Perhaps this is why we understand so well that trust is not the absence of differences."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S094",
            "quote": "Trust is the ability to live with those differences without allowing them to become divisions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "At a time of growing polarization, societies do not become stronger by making everyone the same."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S096",
            "quote": "They become stronger by building institutions in which every single citizen can recognize the same fairness and the same dignity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S097",
            "quote": "Excellencies, the choices we make today, choices on peace, technology, and climate action, will shape the lives of generations yet to come."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "The Pact for the Future reminds us of precisely this responsibility: that the decisions we make today must not undermine the possibilities of those who will live with their consequences tomorrow."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "But future generations should not only be the subject of our decisions; they should have a voice in making them."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "Montenegro has heard the call from young people to move from participation to real influence in decision-making."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "Young people are not simply beneficiaries of public policy; they are partners in shaping it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "Education is our most powerful investment in young people, equipping them with the knowledge, critical thinking, and values they need to shape a better world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "This is very personal to me as well."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "I know what education can make possible."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "I was born and educated in Montenegro."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "It was education that gave me the opportunity to study and work abroad, to learn from other countries and other institutions, and to ultimately return home to serve my own country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "It shaped my belief that the place where a child is born should never define the limits of what that child can become."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "Coming from a small country, one can sometimes assume that greater size brings greater vision and greater wisdom."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "But the United Nations reminds us of a simple truth: vision and wisdom are not measured by the size of a country, but by the ideas we bring and the responsibility with which we act upon them."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "Our responsibility is to expand those possibilities, to build schools that inspire, institutions that recognize talent, economies that reward ideas and work, and societies in which young people have a reason to stay and those who left have a reason to return."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "Artificial intelligence will increasingly shape those possibilities."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S112",
            "quote": "But AI presents not only an extraordinary opportunity; it also creates a responsibility to ensure that technological transformation remains human-centered and rights-based."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S113",
            "quote": "Technology must remain at the service of humanity and not the other way around."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S114",
            "quote": "Climate change demands the same long-term responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S115",
            "quote": "Montenegro carries the identity and responsibility of an ecological state."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S116",
            "quote": "Our mountains, our rivers, our forests, and the Adriatic Sea are not simply natural resources."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S117",
            "quote": "They are part of our national identity and of the legacy we will leave to our future generations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S118",
            "quote": "But climate change is also a question of global fairness, because those who have contributed the least to this crisis are too often the first and hardest hit by its consequences."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S119",
            "quote": "No country can solve this challenge alone."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S120",
            "quote": "This is one of the clearest reasons why effective multilateralism remains indispensable."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
