  "PLW": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Ocean and climate finance",
        "text": "Sought investment in Unlocking Blue Pacific Prosperity and the Pacific Resilience Facility, with grant-based and concessional support that accounts for island vulnerability. Reaffirmed science-based ocean management and a national target to reduce fossil-fuel use by 44% by 2035.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S012",
            "quote": "Pacific leaders have charted a practical roadmap through Unlocking Blue Pacific Prosperity, UBPP, launched at COP28 and reinforced by the Pacific leaders' ocean statement adopted in Palau."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S013",
            "quote": "UBPP unites 22 Pacific countries and territories to mobilize accessible, catalytic investment for 100% sustainable ocean management, robust food systems, resilience, and livelihoods, advancing our shared 30 by 30 commitment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S014",
            "quote": "We continue to seek and expand investment in UBPP to meet its goals and deliver lasting resilience for our communities."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S015",
            "quote": "Palau is translating that UBPP vision into national action."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S016",
            "quote": "We have launched our sustainable ocean policy that commits to 100% effective, science-based, and adaptive management of our ocean, balancing protection with production to deliver the optimal benefits for our people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S017",
            "quote": "In line with this effort, with support from partners like Japan, we are working to develop fishing ports and other critical infrastructure to truly capture the value of resources harvested in our waters."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S018",
            "quote": "As chair of the Pacific Islands Forum and AOSIS, and through Palau's leadership on the High-Level Panel for a Sustainable Ocean Economy, we continue to call for an ocean agenda that meets the scale of this challenge."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S019",
            "quote": "But, Mr."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "President, the task now is delivery."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "We need financing that reaches communities without adding debt, adaptation finance that is accessible to countries already bearing the cost of problems they did not create, and full support for loss and damage and the special circumstances of SIDS."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "This means grant-based and concessional finance, grid readiness and storage, productive energy use, and support that respects our circumstances while enabling delivery at scale."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "Those who contributed the least to this climate crisis, yet confront the worst threats of rising sea levels, must not be burdened with debt simply to purchase a life jacket for their survival."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "International financial institutions must look beyond income and account for vulnerabilities of SIDS."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "Climate exposure, remoteness, narrow economies, and limited access to affordable finance must be considered."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "The Antigua and Barbuda Agenda for SIDS provides a strong roadmap for resilience, but requires urgent, predictable, and scaled-up support."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "The Pacific Resilience Facility is one practical answer: the PRF."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "Endorsed by Pacific leaders, the PRF is the first Pacific-led, owned, and managed regional financing facility dedicated to climate and disaster resilience, and the first international financial institution collectively owned by the Pacific, focused on turning resources into real community-level resilience."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "The PRF reflects the kind of capital the world should support."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "Resilience must also transform how we power our homes, move our people, and connect our islands."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "Energy security is climate security and national security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "Through the Manabara Call to Action, the Pacific reaffirmed a shared vision of 100% renewable energy and a just, inclusive, and equitable transition away from fossil fuels."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "This is not about reducing emissions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "It is about reducing vulnerability to imported fuel, external shocks, and prices we do not control."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "Palau is carrying that regional commitment into national action."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "Our latest commitment targets a 44% reduction in fossil fuel use by 2035, supported by renewable energy generation and practical policies that make the transition affordable and reliable."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Public health proposal",
        "text": "Highlighted a formal request for the Secretary-General to initiate a WHO review of nicotine as a psychotropic substance. Called for stronger prevention, cessation support, and international cooperation to protect young people from dependence.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "Resilience is also about safeguarding public health."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "I commend Palau's First Lady for advancing efforts to combat tobacco and nicotine use with a focus on our youth."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "Her efforts led to the formal request to the UN Secretary-General to initiate a WHO review of nicotine as a psychotropic substance."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "Globally, nicotine claims over 7 million lives annually, with more than a billion trapped in addiction."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "Protecting our future requires expanding prevention, enhancing cessation support, and enacting strong policies to diminish the appeal and affordability of these harmful products."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "No country should have to choose between the health of its children and the commercial interests of an industry that is built on addiction."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "We call for stronger international cooperation to protect young people from nicotine dependence and to put public health before profit."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Maritime and Pacific security",
        "text": "Condemned Iranian actions obstructing navigation through Hormuz and voiced concern over a Chinese ballistic-missile test said to have crossed Pacific states without adequate notice. Rejected treating the Pacific as a venue for strategic competition.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "The Russia-Ukraine war is a painful reminder of the tragic human toll that occurs when diplomacy gives way to conflict and how challenging it is to de-escalate tensions once violence erupts."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "The Strait of Hormuz situation demonstrates how quickly disruption in an important waterway threatens international stability, energy security, and trade worldwide."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "Reaffirming the primary responsibility under the UN Charter to maintain global peace and security, we uphold the sovereignty of Bahrain, Jordan, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, and the UAE, and condemn the actions of Iran to jeopardize maritime security and aim to obstruct, close, and interfere with international navigation through the strait."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "At our Pacific Leaders Meeting in Palau, leaders expressed deep concern that China's ballistic missile test overflew several Pacific nations without adequate notice."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "Let me remind you: our region must never be treated as an empty expanse for strategic competition or a test of military power."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "The Pacific is home to peoples, communities, cultures, fisheries, and ecosystems."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "It is the foundation of our security, the source of our nourishment, and a lifeline for the global community."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "In the face of these risks, the Pacific way is to address tensions before they become crises, make room for dialogue before disagreement becomes conflict, seek inclusion rather than isolation, and uphold respect, restraint, and international law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "The Pacific is our home, not a theater for geopolitical competition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "It must remain an ocean of peace where nations meet in cooperation, international law is respected, and the security of Pacific peoples is never compromised."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Taiwan and sovereignty",
        "text": "Supported Taiwan’s meaningful UN participation and reversal of procedural interpretations that restrict it. Stressed small states’ right to choose partners without coercion and resolve disputes through dialogue and international law.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "Resilience requires partnership shaped by our priorities and respects our sovereignty."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "How we protect our ocean, confront climate change, and power our islands leads directly to how the world engages with us."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "Partnership must never become pressure, and assistance must never come at the cost of the nation's values, institutions, or freedom to choose."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "Sovereignty is not isolation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "It is the freedom to cooperate through mutual respect, transparency, accountability, dialogue, and international law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "In Palau, we say we are a friend to all."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "We choose our partners based on our shared values of democracy, human rights, and a rules-based international order, principles that underpin our friendship with Taiwan, a trusted partner that can contribute even more fully if given the space to do so."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "The UN Charter begins with the commitment, “We the peoples.” Yet the UN marginalizes Taiwan's 23 million people, disregarding that foundational purpose."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "We stand with like-minded partners in calling for the reversal of misinterpretations of the rules and procedures that have constrained Taiwan's meaningful participation in this body."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "Under the UN Charter, small states are sovereign states with the right to determine their own future, choose their partners, and pursue development that serves their people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "We urge all parties to preserve peace and stability, resolve differences peacefully, and choose dialogue over escalation."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
