  "PAN": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Migration and U.S. cooperation",
        "text": "Criticized the UN response to Darién migration and credited Panamanian measures and coordination with the United States for reported declines of 50% in late 2024 and 99% in 2025. Linked irregular movement to trafficking and environmental harm.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S020",
            "quote": "I want to give you a concrete example to illustrate what I am saying."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S021",
            "quote": "Since 2021, this organization has been working on recommendations and calling out illegal migration across the Darién, and it established a humanitarian aid system that looked more like a concentration camp in the midst of the 21st century."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "However, in practical terms, the transit of people increased in 2022, even more in 2023, and during the first six months of 2024."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "Thus, uncontrolled migration turned into massive illegal migration."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "Human trafficking organizations linked to drug trafficking used and abused this space to transport more families, and the result was women and children, with children ending up orphaned in one of the worst social disasters that my country can remember."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "In addition to this, we must add the ecological damage caused in a biodiversity reserve, the Darién Gap Reserve, which has still not recovered."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "This is a situation in which more than a million people were transiting across it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "From the first day, I knew that we needed to resolve this issue ourselves because this organization was not able to do it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "For this reason, at the beginning of my term, I signed a memorandum of understanding with the Government of the United States."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "This, at the end of the day, is also a border issue for the United States, but it was taking place in Panama."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "During the second six months of 2024, with a colossal effort by my country, we managed to oversee a 50% drop compared to the first six months of the year."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "In 2025, when restrictive measures were implemented in the United States and we worked in better coordination with one another, we saw a 99% drop."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "This meant halting one of the worst humanitarian disgraces that Panama has ever seen in its history, putting an end to family separation, and stopping criminals from profiting."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "This description should not be seen as an isolated criticism, but rather as an inflection point to understand the increasingly widening gap between what citizens expect and what they are able to obtain from this organization on issues such as illegal migration, for example."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Canal and environment",
        "text": "Announced the Río Indio reservoir project to support Canal operations and public water supply, and an international initiative recognizing universal rights of nature. Sought support for development projects and recognition of Panama’s stated environmental contribution.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "World trade, without a shadow of a doubt, is one of the best expressions of the freedom to produce, transport, and trade products from one area or nation to another."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "We are proud to be a country that connects the world through trade."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "The Canal, which unites two oceans and transports goods from all countries of the world without any distinction, is an icon of integration."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "This strategic canal for the free world is once again suffering the consequences of climate change."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "This is a real paradox because we are a carbon-negative country and one of the very few carbon-negative countries in the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "But this does not mean that we do not have to face severe droughts followed by heavy rains that cause flooding."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "This leads us to reflect that there is a lot of support for nations that assume the objective of decarbonization."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "But the fact is that we do not benefit from any type of economic aid, despite the fact that we remove more carbon from the world than we produce."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "Therefore, it will be the Panama Canal itself, which grew under Panamanian hands and saw billions of dollars in investments, that will build the Río Indio project."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "This will be a water reservoir to ensure that the Canal can continue to be used, provide more predictability to international trade, and supply water to hundreds of thousands of citizens."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "This is an endeavor for the United Nations to support responsible projects, both socially and environmentally, that represent real progress for our countries."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "It is fundamental not to give in to pressure from organizations that seek extortion under the cover of social struggles and seek shelter in international organizations such as the ILO, for example."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "Distinguished delegates, Panama is a global leader in the conservation of biodiversity and cultural legacy as a basis for our sustainable development."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "We are a country that protects 33% of our territory and 54% of our seas."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "Last year, we announced here our Pact for Nature and the Natural Panama Fund, initiatives on which we are already making progress."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "Today, I am announcing that Panama will lead an international effort to recognize the universal rights of nature."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "I ask all of you to support us in this initiative."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "UN reform and navigation",
        "text": "Called for a permanent Latin American and Caribbean Council seat and more effective preventive diplomacy. Defended Canal neutrality and equal passage, and warned that Hormuz disruption harms food, fertilizer, and energy supplies.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "As heads of state, we know all too well that trust is not something that can be decreed through resolutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "Confidence and trust are won on the ground, when institutions fulfill their promises, when international law is applied without selectivity, and when peoples see that the multilateral system delivers concrete actions and results."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "Just an anecdote: in 1992, when I was a young minister in our country, I participated in Bali, Indonesia, in the first post-Cold War meeting of the Non-Aligned Movement."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "At that time, everything was very vague and difficult, and the world had no better organization for a group of countries like ours."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "We were fighting against apartheid, colonialism, neocolonialism, and disputes in the Middle East."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "At the end of the day, we were fighting against problems across the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "Panama was in the final stages of recovering sovereignty over the Canal, and Ambassador Dr."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "César Cuéllar was here at the United Nations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "What happened then?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "Well, there was a very frank and short response: support us in international public law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "Here we are today, many years later, talking about the same thing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "We firmly believe in useful multilateralism that is not an end in itself, but rather an effective tool to promote the development of peoples and preserve peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "If we take a look now at the Straits of Hormuz, this clearly shows shortcomings in the implementation of international law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "We clearly see the impossibility of providing solutions when crises first arise."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "This is a crisis that is leading to global repercussions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "It would be very easy for me not to speak about this issue because the Panama Canal has benefited as a result of this situation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "But I have never been guided by selfishness or speculation in a matter that is so sensitive for the entire world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "The reality is harmful, not just as a result of the attacks on innocent people, such as vessel crews, but also for millions of people who are running out of food or having to pay more for food and fertilizers, and workers who are having to pay more for fuel as a result of inflation, which is the most regressive phenomenon that exists."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "I feel indignation as a Panamanian."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "We are staunch defenders of sovereignty, after all, and we also have a treaty of neutrality for the Canal, which is in our Constitution and is ultimately the guarantee of free trade and equality of passage for all nations of the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "As you can therefore see, Panama believes in these principles and actively works to ensure that they are applied in practice."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "Next December, our country will finish its mandate as a non-permanent member of the Security Council."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "As we took on this high and lofty task, our premise was clear."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "We did not come to the Council to choose sides."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "We came to the Council to defend principles: sovereignty, territorial integrity, the peaceful settlement of disputes, and the protection of civilians."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "These are the rules that protect the very existence of states, particularly the smallest states."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "I wish to reiterate to this General Assembly the need for Latin America and the Caribbean to have greater decision-making power in the Security Council, specifically a permanent seat for a member of the Security Council of this organization."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "We are a region that plays a leading role in food, minerals, biodiversity, and a deep-seated belief in peace and integration."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "Our contribution is beyond doubt."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "The world does not need less UN; it needs a United Nations that works better, acts with preventive diplomacy, and can yield positive results in the short term."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "We are at a turning point in our history."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "The election of the next Secretary-General will be of paramount importance in determining the next agenda and ensuring robust, lasting trust, of course, in the understanding of the new global balance, if you can call it that."
          }
