      {
        "label": "Venezuela and regional diplomacy",
        "text": "Defended opening dialogue with Venezuelan authorities as support for a pluralistic transition, not endorsement of the government. Sought regional and UN help for Venezuela’s reintegration and democratic institutions, and assistance to Nicaragua, Cuba, and Haiti.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S022",
            "quote": "The first issue that I wish to address here is one that is in my own neighborhood in Latin America."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S023",
            "quote": "Everyone's aware of it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "Its name is Venezuela."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "Before coming to New York, I visited Caracas, despite the fact that diplomatic relations between Paraguay and Venezuela have been suspended."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S026",
            "quote": "My decision to visit the Caribbean country therefore surprised many, and many people have questioned, sometimes harshly, my decision."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "I would therefore like to use this forum to say it loudly and clearly."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "I didn't go to Venezuela to legitimize a regime."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "I did not go there to legitimize or validate anything whatsoever."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "No, ladies and gentlemen, quite the opposite."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "Paraguay cherishes democracy, and we believe that the Venezuelan people also deserve democracy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "The reason I went to Venezuela is because, for 25 years, South American leaders have issued fine lyrical rhetoric, resounding statements, and countless slogans on Venezuela."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "For 25 years, we watched, we waited, and we condemned from the comfort of this distance without doing anything for the Venezuelan people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "We watched, we talked, but we didn't act."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "We did nothing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "In the meantime, our Venezuelan brothers and sisters suffered."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "That is why I went to Venezuela a few days ago: to take a second step following the first difficult but extremely important step that was represented by the fall of the dictator Maduro."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "Because Paraguay can play a useful role in the second step: Venezuela's transition towards a pluralistic democracy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "Venezuela is now facing a new reality."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "Defending our values cannot mean standing indifferent to that reality."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "That is why Paraguay has opened a channel of dialogue with the Venezuelan authorities and is already taking action towards a Venezuela in which power resides with its one true sovereign, the Venezuelan people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "Dialogue doesn't mean abandoning our principles or forgetting the past."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "It means having the courage to look ahead and to act."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "We cannot wait for the United States or some northern power to resolve our problems."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "We have to resolve them ourselves."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "For Venezuela, what I want is what my own country achieved after 35 years of dictatorship in 1989: a real, lasting democratic transition."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "I don't want a photo opportunity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "I don't want to communicate."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "I want, we want, a transition with institutions, with security, with an economy, and with a people that are once again integrated into the international community and, in our region, integrated into Mercosur."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "Paraguayan leadership doesn't confuse dialogue with indifference."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "Dialogue, talking, is one way of standing with the Venezuelan people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "It's also a way of jointly combating transnational crime, which knows no borders and which harms our entire region."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "Today, I call on all my Latin American brothers and sisters, but also on these United Nations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "Let us come together to help Venezuela, this beautiful country, to reintegrate into the world and achieve a democratic government that respects human rights."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "To borrow the words of the Latin poet, Publius: \"I am human, nothing human is alien to me.\"The suffering of the Venezuelan people is also the suffering of the Paraguayan people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "It is the suffering of us all."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "And what applies to Venezuela applies perhaps even more so to Nicaragua, Cuba, and Haiti, countries that have lived for far too long in the darkness of authoritarianism, violence, and sorrow."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "Let us bring light to these sister nations, for where there are free elections, there is hope."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "But we mustn't stop at words."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "We must act."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "Let us do so."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "Let us do so together."
          }
