          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "Hormuz is the problem we face today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "But I wish to tell you here that tomorrow's problem could be far worse, infinitely worse."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "I'm referring to the ominous clouds gathering over the Indo-Pacific, particularly over the Taiwan Strait."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "What happens there is not merely a regional matter."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "No, ladies and gentlemen, it affects Japan, the whole of East and Southeast Asia, and above all, it affects the global economy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "It affects the microchips that power industry, defense, and artificial intelligence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "Anyone pretending that this is far off or too distant to matter simply has not understood the 21st century."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "If oil was the fuel of the 20th century, microchips are the fuel of the 21st."
