      {
        "label": "UN reform and leadership",
        "text": "Called for a more effective, representative Council and a Secretary-General from Latin America and the Caribbean with a stronger preventive-diplomacy role.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "But the world's problems do not end in a single region or place."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "They go to the very heart of the international system."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "The United Nations, and I am neither the first nor the last to say so, needs renewal."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "It needs fresh impetus."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "And the admirable theme of this Assembly calls for a United Nations for all."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "An admirable theme, certainly, but I fear that it's not enough."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "So I ask you today, respectfully but firmly, how can we have a United Nations for all when it is led by a Security Council of the few?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "Worse still, this is a council that was designed 80 years ago for another era, for another scenario, another entire set of circumstances, one that all too often demonstrates it is simply unable to address today's problems."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "That original design, a product of its time, has achieved much, without any doubt."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "And today I recognize and celebrate those achievements; we all should."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "Nonetheless, as the great Nobel laureate Bob Dylan would say, things have changed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "And the organization, dear friends, has to change too."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S112",
            "quote": "Different problems need different solutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S113",
            "quote": "Otherwise, this magnificent idea, the United Nations, will simply be overtaken by events and will be reduced to a forum for beautiful speeches with very little action for ordinary people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S114",
            "quote": "Some have concluded from all of this that multilateralism has failed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S115",
            "quote": "Paraguay reaches a different conclusion."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S116",
            "quote": "The United Nations remains indispensable."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S117",
            "quote": "It is the only system that enables all the countries of the world to coexist, but it must become more effective at preventing conflict, protecting people, and ensuring respect for the rules that states themselves have agreed upon."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S118",
            "quote": "Our commitment to peace is summed up in the words of a distinguished Paraguayan, Manuel Gondra: \"Since we cannot ensure that the just are always strong, we must strive to ensure that the strong are always just.\"Paraguay wishes to shoulder greater responsibilities within the system, but this system as it stands simply isn't working."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S119",
            "quote": "That is why we believe that the selection of the next Secretary-General will be a fundamental decision."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S120",
            "quote": "The time has come for that leadership to come from Latin America and the Caribbean."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S121",
            "quote": "Our region has a vocation for peace, dialogue, and multilateralism, and it has candidates that are capable of taking up that responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S122",
            "quote": "We need a Secretary-General who restores the organization's political leadership, one that strengthens preventive diplomacy, acts before crises become irreversible, and one that listens to the states and the peoples whom this organization serves."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S123",
            "quote": "In short, the Security Council must cease to be a pretty snapshot of the world as it was in 1945."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S124",
            "quote": "It must listen more closely to this Assembly and must not remain paralyzed when peace is threatened."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S125",
            "quote": "We need a UN for 2026 or for 2050, not one for 1945."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S126",
            "quote": "Only then will the United Nations be able to truly deliver for all of its members."
          }
        ]
