  "ESP": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "UN reform and technology",
        "text": "Called for equitable Council representation and abolition of the permanent-member veto, stronger UN bodies and the ICC, renewed nuclear non-proliferation and disarmament, and strict regulation of companies controlling social networks and AI.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "However, with the same belief, I must call out the fact that the majority of the voices that today insist on criticizing the United Nations are not describing its failure."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "What they're doing is trying to cause its failure."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "And I must also say that multilateralism is the best tool that humanity has to manage its diversity and its interdependence, especially in a globalized and multipolar world like the world we're living in today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "And this is why what we need to do is ramp up our trust in this organization."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "We must renew it and strengthen it so that this century it can play the same key role that it played last century."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "And doing this will not be easy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "However, the good news is that all of the guidance we need is right here in the United Nations Charter."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "In this Charter, our forefathers wrote the best chapters: the men and women who saw the world burn."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "And even then, they dared to imagine a better future."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "These men and women laid down their wisdom and their hope in this Charter, and they didn't ask us to keep it in a glass case."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "They asked us to fulfill it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "They asked us to defend it and for us to turn back to it in times of uncertainty and extraordinary difficulty."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "And today is one of those times, and therefore it is our duty to rise to the courage and the ambition present in this text, in the United Nations Charter."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "And this is why, ladies and gentlemen, we need to reform the Security Council so that all of the regions in the world have fair representation and so that we can do away with the right of veto of the permanent members."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "Because, as the UN Charter sets out, no country should be judged in its own case, no matter how powerful it is."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "We therefore need to strengthen all of the other main bodies and reorganise the agencies, funds, and programmes, and provide them with more resources and more executive capacity so that they can have a more decisive impact on the great challenges that beset humanity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "We must strengthen bodies like the International Criminal Court so that they can investigate, prosecute, and punish those that break the rules."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "It took humanity centuries to replace might is right with the rule of law, and we must not be the generation that backtracks on this."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "It's for this very reason that we must rebuild the nuclear non-proliferation and disarmament architecture to avoid a poorly designed security policy bringing us back to another global conflict."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "We must impose strict regulations on the tech oligarchs who control the functioning of social networks and the development of artificial intelligence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "At the end of the day, the future of our children is more important than the pockets of these tech oligarchs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Secretary-General selection",
        "text": "Explicitly called for a woman from Latin America as the next Secretary-General, linking the appointment to regional representation, gender equality, and stronger multilateral leadership.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "Of course, doing all of these things will require compromise, time, strong leadership, being able to build agreements, to listen, to look beyond our known reality, and imagine a better alternative."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "And what I'm advocating for in this leadership is very clear."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "Nine men have served as Secretary-General of this organization in its 80 years of existence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "Now it's time for a woman to serve, a Latin American woman."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "Because, ladies and gentlemen, how can an organization that claims to speak on behalf of the whole of humanity never have had a woman leading the organization?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "How can we represent all of the continents if for three decades we haven't let the third most populated continent have this role?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "The United Nations came into being with the promise that all human beings had their place in this house."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "Therefore, the time has come to fulfill the outstanding half."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "The time has come for a woman from Latin America to become United Nations Secretary-General."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "This is an historic debt that we must settle."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "And today, more than ever, when feminism is being attacked, when thousands of women are falling victim to machismo, violence, and xenophobia, we must reaffirm this commitment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "And I want to be very clear: I'm not saying this because I think that women have anything to prove."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "I'm saying it because it is the world that needs to show itself that, on the road to equality, there's no going back."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "In my country, ladies and gentlemen, in Spain, it was women who were the first to show us that security could not be achieved through force, but through social progress."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "It was brave women like Clara Campoamor, the first to defend in Parliament the rejection of war as a way of interacting with the world and opting instead for empathy and peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "That should always be what we do."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "If only more of the leaders that came up to this rostrum this week had even half the courage and lucidity of Clara Campoamor."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "Feminism, ladies and gentlemen, is one of the main forces of transformation and progress that the world has experienced in the last century, and it's time for this force to guide this institution in a much clearer and more robust way."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "And it's for these reasons, ladies and gentlemen, that I believe that in order to get off on the right footing in this new decisive step forward for the United Nations, the UN needs a female Latin American Secretary-General."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "And I believe, what's more, that in order for her not to be alone, she will also need the support of brave governments who are prepared to do things right, however high the price to pay may be."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Conflict and military policy",
        "text": "Reaffirmed opposition to wars of aggression and refused a 5%-of-GDP military-spending target. Cited sanctions on Russia, an arms embargo on Israel’s government, and restrictions on use of Spanish territory for attacks; accused Israel’s government of genocide in Gaza.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "This, ladies and gentlemen, is the option and the way forward that Spain has chosen."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "Over the last eight years, my country has opposed all wars of aggression wherever they have started, whether it's in Ukraine, in Lebanon, or in Iran."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "We have refused to increase our military spending to 5% of GDP, and we've done everything possible to avoid aggressions that run counter to the UN Charter: placing sanctions on the Russian aggressors, imposing an arms embargo on the Netanyahu government in Israel, prohibiting the use of our territory to deploy an aggression that was against international law, and unequivocally condemning the genocide that Netanyahu is still perpetrating in Gaza."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Aid and migration",
        "text": "Reported increased development and multilateral contributions despite wider aid cuts. Reaffirmed the SDGs and said the response to migration pressures in Ceuta should uphold law and human rights rather than portray migrants as enemies.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "We have also mobilised resources to do more."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "In the face of the chainsaws that have cut close to a third of world development aid in just two years, Spain has doubled its investment in cooperation and has increased its contribution to the multilateral system by 60%."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "And we've done this always holding true to our principles, not even in the most difficult times, like the times being experienced by the Spanish city of Ceuta, where inequality, desperation, and disinformation have fed one of the most significant irregular migration crises in recent years."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "I know that in times like this, the temptation is to take shortcuts, to give in to fear, to turn migrants into the enemy, and to break the law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "However, my country, Spain, will not do this, and a Spanish city like Ceuta won't do it either, because their citizens are showing that we can tackle a crisis without compromising on decency, upholding the law, and respecting human rights."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "And we'll come out of this stronger precisely for this reason, because Spain does not choose the easy route."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "We always choose the fairest route."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "And I also want to recognize that the world knows this."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "At the end of the day, the reactionary forces that want to destroy this multilateral order won't stop attacking us for it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "They want us to be intimidated, they want us to give up, they want us to end up believing that the SDGs are a lost cause, that defending the common good is naive, that cooperating is an act of weakness."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "Well, I'm here and I've come up to this rostrum to tell you loud and clear that they are wrong and that we will not keep quiet."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S094",
            "quote": "The Spanish people are not going back."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "We will not stop believing that humanity can continue to progress and that, working together, we can build a better world."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
