  "TLS": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Nuclear initiative",
        "text": "Urged President Trump to convene nuclear-armed states, major military powers, and defense industries to establish no-first-strike commitments, regular communications, and a decade-long path toward reducing and eliminating nuclear arsenals.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S027",
            "quote": "Russia, the US, China, France, and the UK, all members of the NPT, were joined by four countries not members of the NPT: Israel, India, Pakistan, and North Korea."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S028",
            "quote": "Yes, North Korea has a nuclear arsenal, estimated to be around 100."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S029",
            "quote": "And North Korean leaders seem to have learned lessons from Libya, Ukraine, and the ongoing Iran-Israel war."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S030",
            "quote": "Dismantle your nuclear capabilities, and you lose the only deterrent you have against a nuclear power deciding to bomb you into submission."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S031",
            "quote": "On June 30, 2019, President Trump traveled to the DMZ on the Korean Peninsula."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S032",
            "quote": "The mysterious, Swiss-educated leader of North Korea, half the age of the American president, walked halfway, and the two leaders engaged in an embrace that promised peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "This is what leaders do to advance peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "They show courage and audacity."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "President Trump, you did the right thing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "Friends are friends; we cherish and embrace our friends, never ignoring them or excluding them from the table."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S037",
            "quote": "But we talk to adversaries so that we do not become enemies."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S038",
            "quote": "We talk to enemies to prevent wars, and perhaps we become partners in peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S039",
            "quote": "Those countries amassing nuclear weapons keep us all living near imminent catastrophe."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S040",
            "quote": "One day, any day, by accident, miscalculation, computer error, madness, or foolish strategic design, we could become the last human generation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S041",
            "quote": "All the while, the brandishing of these weapons reinforces adversity and fear, which create a high barrier to achieving the rational cooperation necessary to fulfill our responsibility to future generations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "Trillions of dollars are invested in perfecting forms of death."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "Instead, we invest a fraction of these trillions in clean water, food, schools, and clinics."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "No thought was given to the tens of millions of fellow human beings pushed back into extreme deprivation by COVID-19 and the Ukraine-Russia war."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "And as if innocent bystanders on the periphery had not suffered enough, we are presented with another catastrophe: the Iran war and disruption of vital waterways for trade."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "We know the madness of Iranian leaders seeking regional supremacy, pouring fuel into the fire of religious extremism in neighboring countries to destabilize wealthy, stable monarchies."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "Iranian leaders launched unwarranted attacks against neighbors, destroying civilian industries and infrastructure."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "Iran’s rationale for this attack is that those countries host American bases."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "So is Iran going to launch waves of drones and missiles against U."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "S. bases in Europe?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "Can we change course?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "Can we stop sleepwalking into wider wars?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "My invitation to President Trump: be audacious, be unpredictable, be visionary."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "Invite all nuclear powers and all major conventional military powers and industries, without exception, to a summit somewhere, maybe in a town in Portugal, to talk about no first strike and, hence, regular communication between leaders of the nuclear powers."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "Commit to the reduction of nuclear weapons towards total deactivation and destruction of nuclear arsenals over a decade."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Regional diplomacy",
        "text": "Condemned Iran’s attacks on neighboring states, welcomed U.S. humanitarian assistance to Cuba, and supported a two-state solution. Described Morocco’s Western Sahara proposal as an opportunity for a negotiated settlement that consults the people directly concerned.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "And as if innocent bystanders on the periphery had not suffered enough, we are presented with another catastrophe: the Iran war and disruption of vital waterways for trade."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "We know the madness of Iranian leaders seeking regional supremacy, pouring fuel into the fire of religious extremism in neighboring countries to destabilize wealthy, stable monarchies."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "Iranian leaders launched unwarranted attacks against neighbors, destroying civilian industries and infrastructure."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "Iran’s rationale for this attack is that those countries host American bases."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "So is Iran going to launch waves of drones and missiles against U."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "S. bases in Europe?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "The humanitarian situation in Cuba is heartbreaking."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "We understand that the US has provided 100 million in emergency humanitarian assistance to Cuba through Caritas."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "In keeping with the U."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "S. humanitarian tradition, we hope this will create an environment conducive to normal, long-term Cuba-U."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "S. relations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "Trade relations between Cuba and the U."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "S., and the rest of the world, could be improved."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "Regarding the situation in the Israeli-occupied territories, Gaza and the West Bank, Timor-Leste joins with the vast majority of UN Member States to reaffirm our belief that the two-state solution is the only viable solution for Israelis to live in peace with themselves and with the Palestinians, and for the Palestinians to live in peace with themselves and with the Israelis."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "The risks are too high to continue an unstable status quo."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "The opportunity to do better sits before us, and the choice is an international order falling to pieces or rising to peace."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "Regarding Western Sahara, we welcome the Moroccan proposal and the recent Security Council resolution as an opportunity for dialogue."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "As with any situation of this nature, the people directly interested must be consulted on the future status."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "We hope that a just, comprehensive settlement is reached between Moroccan authorities and the Polisario Front."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "UN reform",
        "text": "Called for a woman from Latin America as the next Secretary-General, expansion of both Security Council membership categories, and reform of the veto. Said efficiency measures must preserve essential support to developing countries.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S118",
            "quote": "Soon we will elect a new Secretary-General."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S119",
            "quote": "The regional rotation precedent must be preserved."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S120",
            "quote": "Africa had an unprecedented continuous three-term tenure: Boutros Boutros-Ghali, 1992–1996; Kofi Annan, 1997–2006."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S121",
            "quote": "Now the Security Council will elect a Latin American as our Secretary-General for 2027–2032."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S122",
            "quote": "And after more than 80 years of men at the helm of our Organization, needless to say, we ought to have enough wisdom and elect a woman with unquestionable integrity, an unblemished record, and, in the field of human rights, a strong advocate of gender equality and inclusion, the rule of law, democracy, and solid experience in senior management in national and multilateral institutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S124",
            "quote": "President, Excellencies, for developing countries, particularly small island developing states and least developed countries, efficiency must translate into stronger delivery on the ground, not reduced essential support."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S125",
            "quote": "Timor-Leste urges comprehensive reform, expansion in both the permanent and non-permanent categories, so that developing countries and historically underrepresented regions have a stronger voice in decisions concerning international peace and security."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S126",
            "quote": "The veto is inconsistent with the sovereign equality of Member States."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Development and inclusion",
        "text": "Sought predictable climate finance, technology transfer, and developing-country participation in AI governance. Reaffirmed ASEAN centrality and balanced relations with major powers while urging greater attention to neglected humanitarian crises.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "Excellencies, please take some time to look at the situation in Sudan, the worst humanitarian crisis in the world today."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "Look at the situation in South Sudan, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Afghanistan, Myanmar, and Yemen."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "These are not abstract."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "They are people; they are women, they are children, youth in their best years, they are parents, they are grandparents."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "And they are a grand jury of humanity, indicting us all, leaders and businesses of death."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "For you are celebrating the tens of billions of dollars in profit from wars and death that you are accomplices to."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "How is it that we can scroll past the end of the world before finishing our coffee?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "How is it that a child pulling pieces of his family from the rubble has become a headline, so we quickly skip a notification with silence?"
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "A Tuesday."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "Behind each of the dead is not a statistic."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "It is a mother who will spend the rest of her life searching for a face in a crowd that will never appear."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "It is a boy hiding in silence, learning before he can read that the world outside his door wants him dead."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "It is a girl, pregnant by the man who came to destroy her home, carrying inside her both the violence done to her and the life she never chose."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "We tell ourselves we would never look away if we truly saw it."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "And yet we saw Rwanda and Bosnia happen right under UN watch."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "We see it every day, live in our pockets, in vivid color."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "And still, somehow, life goes on normally."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "We finish our meetings, we plan our weekends, we grow inured to the killings of Palestinians."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "This is not a lack of information."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "We are drowning in information."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "We can live-stream as it all happens."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "This is a lack of feeling and a numbness we have allowed to settle over us like dust."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "All this happened before our eyes, but from the powers that can make the difference between life and death, there is no response."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S094",
            "quote": "And worse, we witness diplomatic acrobatics to brush off the bombing of a school or a hospital, saying that it does not really violate international law because the terrorists, quote unquote, may be hiding in the basement of the building."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "I am worried."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S096",
            "quote": "Worried that we have started treating a catastrophe as something we can simply coexist with."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S097",
            "quote": "Worried that the killing of civilians is casually being justified."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "Worried that total force now sounds more viable than diplomacy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "This very institution was founded on a promise."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "All through the archives here, resolutions say a ceasefire must hold, a border must not be crossed, a civilian must not be a target."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "Many of those promises remain unmet, raising concern that the phrase “never again” has lost meaning."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "I do not have a plan that will end a war by tonight, but I know this: numbness is not neutral."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "Silence is not safety."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "Every time we let the suffering of people become background noise, we let ourselves forget how small the distance really is, how little separates your daughter, granddaughter, niece, from the girl in the refugee camp you saw on the news last night, how many children right now are learning that a world at war is normality."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "The more we linger in this fog, the harder it becomes for the hiding child to believe the world is not his enemy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "These tragedies are not somebody else’s tragedy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "They are what we allowed, what we still allow, and what we will answer for."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S127",
            "quote": "President, Timor-Leste reaffirms the principles of climate justice, common but differentiated responsibilities, and respective capabilities in the light of different national circumstances."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S128",
            "quote": "Greater climate ambition must be accompanied by accessible, predictable finance, adaptation support, technology transfer, and capacity building."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S129",
            "quote": "Artificial intelligence and other emerging technologies reshape our societies."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S130",
            "quote": "Developing countries must actively participate in their governance and development."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S137",
            "quote": "President, our accession to ASEAN on 26 October 2025 was a historic moment for our country, marking the culmination of a 14-year process that began when Timor-Leste formally applied for membership in March 2011."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S139",
            "quote": "President, our accession to ASEAN on 26 October 2025 was a historic moment for our country, marking the culmination of a 14-year process that began when Timor-Leste formally applied for membership in March 2011."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S140",
            "quote": "Fellow ASEAN leaders have generously provided us with technical assistance, capacity building, and practical guidance, and they continue to do so."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S141",
            "quote": "It requires of us strong institutions, capable public servants, and effective implementation of ASEAN commitments across political, security, economic, and social-cultural communities."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S142",
            "quote": "Our foreign policy seeks friendship with all and hostility toward none."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S143",
            "quote": "We aim to maintain balanced, constructive relations with all major powers and development partners."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S144",
            "quote": "Timor-Leste also brings the energy and aspiration of a young population."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S145",
            "quote": "Our young people are increasingly connected to the region and eager to learn, work, and contribute."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S146",
            "quote": "As ASEAN works towards Community Vision 2045, Timor-Leste will support a united, people-centred, and resilient ASEAN."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S147",
            "quote": "We will also support ASEAN centrality and constructive relations with all external partners."
