  "VEN": {
    "bullets": [
      {
        "label": "Political transition",
        "text": "Announced what she described as an orderly, institutional, verifiable transition, including judicial reform, opposition dialogue, and elections with equal participation. The speech gave no election date and left timing to Venezuelan processes; implementation is not established by the announcement.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S064",
            "quote": "I come before this assembly as one more daughter of Venezuela to present the aspirations of a country that is seeking to rebuild its own destiny following political conflicts and economic models that were imposed and affected our development."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S065",
            "quote": "For all too long, we were a divided country, a country in which the colour of a party flag held more weight than the common surname that we all share, that is the name Venezuelan."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S066",
            "quote": "This stage must conclude to usher in a new political era based in truth, justice, and the ability to look forward together and to find, in political dialogue underpinned by respect, a genuine forum within which we can settle the differences which we have as Venezuelans, seeking always in so doing to forge ahead for the well-being of the country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S067",
            "quote": "I am delighted to announce that Venezuela has begun a process of democratic transition to ensure its rebirth."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S068",
            "quote": "This is an orderly, institutional, verifiable process to build a country that is freer for all, more prosperous, and more at peace with itself."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S069",
            "quote": "This is a process of political, economic, and spiritual change and a time of structural reforms to ensure Venezuela's rebirth, the rebirth of our nation and our people."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S070",
            "quote": "We are seeking here to build a country in which no one has to win by riding roughshod over someone else or ignoring them, because all of us, particularly young people who are entering political life for the first time, are Venezuela."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S071",
            "quote": "We must aspire to a Venezuela whose political class is deeply committed to the national interest, placing it above anything else."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S072",
            "quote": "And this political class must not be held hostage by media algorithms."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S073",
            "quote": "I know Venezuela intimately."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S074",
            "quote": "I thank God for the opportunity he has provided me with to experience institutional forums which exist within various sectors of public life."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S075",
            "quote": "I know where the doors are, doors that must open to usher in a wholesale transformation of Venezuela, and doors through which we must walk to establish a new basis for an economy which serves development at a national level, and what we must do to ensure full justice for all regardless of social or political class."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S076",
            "quote": "And I know what we must do to develop a justice system and a system of social equality as foreseen by the father of our liberation, Simón Bolívar."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S077",
            "quote": "I want us to arise from the rubble and establish the foundations of a new, diverse, deeply spiritual nation, a new republic which is at peace with itself."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S078",
            "quote": "However, the world is increasingly less integrated and more polarised."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S079",
            "quote": "The world has taught us that some of the most solid democratic transitions of the modern world were not born from fracture or breakdowns, but from a transformation spearheaded with iron resolve by institutions themselves."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S080",
            "quote": "This is our inspiration."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S081",
            "quote": "We do not seek to reproduce a trajectory which belongs to another nation or the past, but we want to move forward on the basis of a universal idea."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S082",
            "quote": "Abiding by the law can serve as a path towards better, stronger law."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S083",
            "quote": "A nation cannot only be reborn by rebuilding buildings; it is reborn when it rebuilds trust in its institutions."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S084",
            "quote": "Consequently, I wish to announce and reaffirm in unambiguous terms the pillars of this process."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S085",
            "quote": "One, there will be an orderly legal transition and a transition of the judiciary."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S086",
            "quote": "We have embarked upon an institutional review process to ensure the state can grow stronger and to provide legal security which national and international investors require, but which is also required by our citizens."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S087",
            "quote": "They must not feel trampled upon and dictated to by arbitrary powers."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S088",
            "quote": "The judiciary must be at their service."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S089",
            "quote": "We cannot postpone this process."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S090",
            "quote": "There needs to be the responsible exercise of politics."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S091",
            "quote": "Venezuela will guarantee that there can be real participation of all political forces in the country in political life."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S092",
            "quote": "Democracy is not measured by the very existence of elections."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S093",
            "quote": "Democracy is measured by the quality of the competition which occurs before the election."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S094",
            "quote": "An election must serve as a solution, not a generator of irreconcilable conflicts."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S095",
            "quote": "I wish to say the following loud and clear at this General Assembly."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S096",
            "quote": "In Venezuela, there will be elections."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S097",
            "quote": "And in that vein, we have begun a political dialogue with sectors of the opposition which will lead to a process where everyone will compete on an equal footing."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S098",
            "quote": "The Venezuelan people, with their age-old wisdom, will determine when the correct time for these elections is, and Venezuelan institutions will be prepared to guarantee that this inclusive and transparent process takes place."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "Ours will be a country that is not submitted to economic restrictions of any kind so that our right to development can be guaranteed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "These knee-jerk reactions that we see from outside the country will be consigned to the theatre of the past, which, as Venezuelans, we no longer wish to see."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "Venezuela must abandon the course which allowed extremism and intolerance to be imposed and to prevail over peaceful and democratic coexistence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "And here, I ask for the support of the international community so that it, in good faith, supports the changes that Venezuela requires."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "It must respect the self-determination of my country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "Venezuela wishes to breathe freely, exercise its rights as a sovereign nation without any type of interference."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "United States and recovery",
        "text": "Thanked President Trump for renewed diplomatic engagement and highlighted a recent U.S.–Venezuelan energy agreement. Sought cooperation on energy, security, transnational crime, and economic development, and thanked partners for assistance after the reported 24 June earthquake.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S024",
            "quote": "Here, I wish to point to the recent agreement signed between the United States and Venezuela as one of the most all-encompassing and significant ever signed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S025",
            "quote": "It will contribute to ensuring the energy security of the hemisphere and the well-being of our economy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S042",
            "quote": "I come to this rostrum to talk to you about a Venezuela whose national life has been affected by a crisis that has disrupted political coexistence, a crisis that disrupted national life and upset our relationships with the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S043",
            "quote": "Interests alien to the common good of the Venezuelan people were pursued without our say-so."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S044",
            "quote": "In 2026, Venezuela was forced to face two major painful tests in its life as a nation."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S045",
            "quote": "One was the test that arose from the suffocation of its internal political life and a dispute with the United States of America, which was ratcheted up and became more extreme."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S046",
            "quote": "Another test arose from nature's savagery."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S047",
            "quote": "That was the double earthquake on the 24th of June."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S048",
            "quote": "In spite of these life's bitter blows, as they were called by the poet César Vallejo, for all of Venezuela's people, Venezuela today is being reborn."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S049",
            "quote": "The idea of our country being reborn is, if you like the expression, our country's attitude, the attitude that it has assumed in the face of the aforementioned events."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S050",
            "quote": "We are transforming our political relationships, and these are now rooted in dialogue, negotiations, and diplomacy."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S051",
            "quote": "We wish to have with the United States, with our neighbours, and with all countries on the continent, relations with the international community."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S052",
            "quote": "We wish to rebuild them and maintain them."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S053",
            "quote": "They must be rooted in respect and equality."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S054",
            "quote": "I wish, before the 81st General Assembly of the United Nations, to thank President Donald Trump and his government for their readiness to resume the course of diplomatic relations and cooperation with Venezuela."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S055",
            "quote": "The last time that two presidents, the President of Venezuela and the President of the United States, met together was in 2009."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S056",
            "quote": "Today, we are working solemnly to settle our differences through dialogue."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S057",
            "quote": "But first and foremost, we are working to pave the way for cooperation in the field of energy, to promote security, and to fight transnational crime together."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S058",
            "quote": "We are looking to buttress economic cooperation for the benefit of our two peoples and the peoples of our continent and the continent as a whole."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S059",
            "quote": "Elsewhere, we are looking to ensure the material, moral, and spiritual recovery of our homeland, which has been beset by a devastating natural disaster."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S060",
            "quote": "I wish to thank all of the countries of America, Europe, Asia, Africa, and the Middle East, as well as the United Nations system as a whole."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S061",
            "quote": "I wish to thank you all."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S062",
            "quote": "You provided your solidarity and your support to the Venezuelan people during the darkest hours of our history that we endured as a result of this double earthquake."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S063",
            "quote": "Here, Venezuela felt the real spirit that inspired the creation of this organisation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Essequibo and sovereignty",
        "text": "Reasserted Venezuela’s claim over the Essequibo territory and called on Guyana to return to bilateral negotiations under the Geneva Agreement. Requested international support that respects Venezuela’s self-determination and opposed external interference.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "sentence_id": "S033",
            "quote": "I would be remiss if I did not make mention here, at the very headquarters of international law, of our desire to reaffirm the historic rights of Venezuela over Guyana Essequibo."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S034",
            "quote": "Here, I appeal to the Cooperative Republic of Guyana to resolve the issue and to return to negotiations as stipulated by the Geneva Agreement."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S035",
            "quote": "Agreements which last the longest are those that emerge from bilateral negotiations."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S036",
            "quote": "They last longer and function better than those imposed by external bodies."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S099",
            "quote": "Ours will be a country that is not submitted to economic restrictions of any kind so that our right to development can be guaranteed."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S100",
            "quote": "These knee-jerk reactions that we see from outside the country will be consigned to the theatre of the past, which, as Venezuelans, we no longer wish to see."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S101",
            "quote": "Venezuela must abandon the course which allowed extremism and intolerance to be imposed and to prevail over peaceful and democratic coexistence."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S102",
            "quote": "And here, I ask for the support of the international community so that it, in good faith, supports the changes that Venezuela requires."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S103",
            "quote": "It must respect the self-determination of my country."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S104",
            "quote": "Venezuela wishes to breathe freely, exercise its rights as a sovereign nation without any type of interference."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S105",
            "quote": "Venezuela must be admired and respected."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S106",
            "quote": "I come here and will do justice going forward."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S107",
            "quote": "That is, I will assume a historic responsibility."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S108",
            "quote": "That is the responsibility of taking Venezuela from uncertainty and conflict to a full democracy which is recognised by its own people and the world."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S109",
            "quote": "This will be a new era of well-being from which Venezuela will be reborn."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S110",
            "quote": "To my beloved people, I wish to say this is not the end of a speech; it is the beginning of a commitment."
          },
          {
            "sentence_id": "S111",
            "quote": "I wish to say to the international community, Venezuela is ready to walk hand in hand with those who believe in respectful international relations, relationships which exist without prejudice or interference."
          }
        ]
